      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The flagged range (lines 98-134) corresponds to the private `search(LDAPPerson person)` method. The only externally-influenced value reaching an LDAP sink in this range is `person.getName()`, which is concatenated into the search filter string at line 108-111: `\"(&(objectclass=person)(uid=\" + ESAPI_Encoder.encodeForLDAP(person.getName()) + \"))\"`. Before concatenation, the value is passed through `ESAPI_Encoder.encodeForLDAP(...)`, which is the OWASP ESAPI encoder specifically designed to escape LDAP filter metacharacters (*, (, ), \\, NUL) for this exact sink type (LDAP search filter). The resulting `filter` string is then passed to `ctx.search(base, filter, sc)`. Because the encoder is applied directly to the attacker-controlled value before it enters the filter and is used for this specific sink (search filter, not DN), the sink is adequately protected. Note: the `insert()` method (lines 67-90) does build an LDAP DN by raw concatenation of `person.getName()` without using the encoder, which could be a separate injection vector, but that code falls outside the flagged line range (98-134) and is not the sink identified by this specific finding.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "medium"
      }
    },
