        "exploitability_evidence": "Attacker-controlled source: cookie 'BenchmarkTest00002' value is read via request.getCookies(), URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) into 'param' with no path validation. It flows directly into fileName = Utils.TESTFILES_DIR + param, which is passed unmodified into new java.io.FileOutputStream(fileName, false) \u2014 the flagged sink. The only sanitizer present, ESAPI encoder().encodeForHTML(fileName), is applied afterward purely for the HTTP response text (HTML-encoding for display), not for the file path itself, and HTML-encoding provides no protection against '../' path traversal sequences in a filesystem path. No canonicalization, no FilenameUtils.getName(), no whitelist/blacklist check on 'param' occurs before it reaches FileOutputStream.",
