          "signal:command_injection": 0.3,
          "taint_source": 0.1,
          "source_sink_combo": 0.2
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest00006\") (line ~45) is attacker-controlled (HTTP header value). It is URL-decoded via java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") (no sanitization for shell metacharacters, just decoding). The decoded value is then concatenated directly into a shell command string: argList.add(\"echo \" + param), which is passed to ProcessBuilder along with \"sh\"/\"-c\" (or cmd.exe /c on Windows). pb.start() executes this via a shell, meaning any shell metacharacters (;, |, &, $(), backticks, etc.) in the header value will be interpreted by the shell, enabling command injection. The only downstream processing (Utils.printOSCommandResults) applies ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML() to the command's stdout/stderr for safe HTML rendering \u2014 that is output encoding for XSS prevention, not input sanitization for the exec sink, and it happens after the command has already run. No validation, whitelist, or escaping of param occurs before it is embedded in the shell command line.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Unsanitized HTTP header value is concatenated into a shell command string ('echo ' + param) and executed via ProcessBuilder with sh -c / cmd.exe /c, allowing shell metacharacters in user input to be interpreted by the shell.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands by supplying shell metacharacters in the 'BenchmarkTest00006' HTTP header, potentially leading to full command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process (data exfiltration, remote code execution, lateral movement).",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with user-supplied data; instead pass the command and arguments as separate list elements to ProcessBuilder without shell interpretation.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, strictly whitelist/validate the input against an allow-list of expected characters (e.g., alphanumeric only) and reject anything else.",
          "Use a dedicated escaping library for shell arguments or avoid building command strings via concatenation altogether.",
          "Apply the principle of least privilege to the process executing the command to limit the impact of a successful injection."
        ]
      }
    },
