      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest00006\") (fully attacker-controlled HTTP header). It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not sanitize shell metacharacters, then concatenated: argList.add(\"echo \" + param). The argList (e.g. [\"sh\",\"-c\",\"echo \"+param]) is passed to pb.command(argList) and pb.start() executes it via a shell (sh -c '...' or cmd.exe /c). Because the tainted value is placed inside a shell -c string, any shell metacharacters (;, |, `, $()) in the header value are interpreted by the shell, enabling arbitrary command injection. No validation, allow-listing, or escaping is applied to param before it is embedded in the command string. The downstream Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the *output* for the response, which has no effect on the command that has already executed.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header value is decoded and directly concatenated into a shell command string (\"echo \" + param) which is executed via ProcessBuilder using a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) without any sanitization, validation, or escaping of shell metacharacters.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands by supplying shell metacharacters in the 'BenchmarkTest00006' HTTP header, leading to remote code execution with the privileges of the web application process, potentially resulting in full system compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell to run commands built from user input; use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and pass user data only as a discrete argument (e.g., ProcessBuilder(\"echo\", param)) without going through sh -c or cmd.exe /c.",
          "If shell interpretation is required, strictly validate/allow-list the input (e.g., alphanumeric only) and reject or encode any shell metacharacters before use.",
          "Use ESAPI or similar OS-command encoders/validators designed for command contexts (not HTML encoding) to sanitize the input.",
          "Run the subprocess with the least privilege necessary and consider sandboxing to limit the impact of any injected commands."
        ]
      }
    },
