        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP header value is URL-decoded and used unsanitized to build a java.io.File path; no path traversal validation (canonicalization, whitelist, or filename-only extraction) is performed before the value reaches the File constructor.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the header value to include directory traversal sequences (e.g., '../') to probe or reference arbitrary paths on the filesystem via the fileTarget.exists() check, potentially enabling information disclosure about the file system structure or, if the code were extended to read/write, arbitrary file access.",
        "remediation": [
