          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled HTTP Referer header is URL-decoded and directly passed to response.getWriter().format() without sanitization, enabling XSS injection.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.423
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") - an attacker-controlled HTTP header. The first header value is extracted into 'param', then URL-decoded via java.net.URLDecoder.decode (no HTML sanitization). This decoded, attacker-controlled string is then passed directly as the format string to response.getWriter().format(param, obj). Any literal (non-format-specifier) content in 'param', including HTML/JS payloads such as <script>alert(1)</script>, is written verbatim to the HTTP response body without any HTML encoding or escaping. No sanitizer, validator, or output encoder is applied anywhere on this path before the writer sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP Referer header value is URL-decoded and written directly to the response writer via Writer.format() without any HTML-encoding or output sanitization, allowing injected markup/script to be reflected into the page.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a request with a malicious Referer header (or induce a victim's browser/proxy to send one) containing HTML/JavaScript; when reflected into the response, this results in reflected Cross-Site Scripting, allowing script execution in the victim's browser session context (session theft, defacement, phishing, etc.).",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the Referer value before writing it to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or a JSP/JSF templating engine that auto-escapes).",
          "Avoid using raw user input as a format string for Writer.format()/String.format(); treat it strictly as data, not as a format template.",
          "Adopt a view/templating technology (JSP with JSTL c:out, JSF, Thymeleaf) that automatically escapes output instead of writing directly to the response OutputStream/Writer.",
          "Set a strict Content-Security-Policy header to reduce impact of any residual XSS.",
          "Do not reflect the Referer header into responses unless absolutely necessary; if required, validate/allow-list its format first."
        ]
      }
    },
