        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: `request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00015\")` retrieves an attacker-controlled HTTP header value into `param`. It is URL-decoded (`URLDecoder.decode`) which does not neutralize shell metacharacters. `param` is then concatenated into `\"echo \" + param` and added as a single argument to `argList`, which is passed to `pb.command(argList)` where argList[0]/[1] are `sh -c` (or `cmd.exe /c`). Because the command is executed via `sh -c \"echo <param>\"`, any shell metacharacters (e.g. `; | & $() \\`` ) in the header value are interpreted by the shell, enabling injection of arbitrary commands. No sanitization, whitelist, or escaping is applied to `param` before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink. The downstream `Utils.printOSCommandResults` only HTML-encodes the *output* of the command for the response, which does not mitigate the injection into the command itself.",
