        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: attacker-controlled HTTP header 'BenchmarkTest00015' via request.getHeaders(...).nextElement(). It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not neutralize shell metacharacters. The value is concatenated into a command string 'echo ' + param, added to argList, and executed via ProcessBuilder with 'sh -c <concatenated string>' (or 'cmd.exe /c'). Since the argument passed to sh -c is a full shell command line built by string concatenation, any shell metacharacters (;, |, `` ` ``, $(), &&, etc.) in the header value will be interpreted by the shell, allowing arbitrary command injection. No sanitization/validation of param against shell-injection is performed before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink.",
