        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00018\") returns attacker-controlled HTTP header value, assigned to 'param'. It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not neutralize SQL metacharacters like single quotes. The decoded param is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + param + \"')\". This string is then executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement obtained from DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement() (not a PreparedStatement with parameter binding). No sanitizer, escaping, or parameterization is applied anywhere on this path before reaching the SQL execution sink. The only encoding downstream (ESAPI encodeForHTML in outputUpdateComplete) is applied to the sql string only for HTML output display, not before the SQL execution, so it does not mitigate the injection.",
