      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The flagged sink at line 54 is response.getWriter().println(\"Your results are: \" + String.valueOf(results)). The value written, 'results', is a Long returned from the JDBC query (queryForObject(sql, Long.class)), not the raw user-controlled request parameter 'param'. While 'param' is concatenated unsanitized into the SQL string (a SQL injection issue), the only value ever written to the HTTP response at this sink is a Long numeric ID converted via String.valueOf(), which cannot carry HTML/script content regardless of what an attacker manipulates via SQL injection. The other catch blocks in this method that do include the raw 'sql' string (which contains param) explicitly HTML-encode it via ESAPI's encodeForHTML before writing to the response. Therefore no attacker-controlled string reaches the writer unescaped at the flagged line.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The scanner flagged use of response.getWriter() as a generic unescaped-output sink, but the actual data written at the flagged line is a numeric Long derived from a database query result, not the tainted request parameter itself. There is no reflected XSS at this specific sink.",
        "impact": "None for XSS at this location since output is constrained to a numeric value; the real vulnerability present in this code is SQL injection via unsanitized concatenation of 'param' into the SQL string, but that is a separate CWE (CWE-89) not covered by this XSS finding.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries/PreparedStatement instead of string concatenation to prevent SQL injection.",
          "If any raw SQL or user input must be echoed back to the client, continue using an HTML encoder (as already done with ESAPI encodeForHTML in the catch blocks) consistently on all output paths.",
          "Avoid directly writing to response.getWriter(); prefer a templating/view layer that auto-escapes output."
        ]
      }
    },
