      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() retrieves 'BenchmarkTest00032' parameter values into `param` (attacker-controlled, no validation). This value is directly concatenated into a SQL string: `\"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + param + \"'\"`. This raw `sql` string is then passed to `DatabaseHelper.JDBCtemplate.execute(sql)`, which executes it as a SQL statement (Spring JdbcTemplate.execute(String) runs the raw SQL with no parameter binding). The only encoding applied \u2014 `ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(sql)` \u2014 is applied AFTER the query has already been executed, and only for safely rendering the query text back to the HTTP response; it does not sanitize the value before it reaches the SQL sink. There is no parameterized query, PreparedStatement, or input validation on the path from source to sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into a SQL query string without parameterization or sanitization before being executed via JdbcTemplate.execute(String).",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the 'BenchmarkTest00032' parameter, potentially bypassing authentication, exfiltrating data, or modifying/deleting data in the USERS table depending on database permissions.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries (PreparedStatement or JdbcTemplate.update/query with '?' placeholders and bound arguments) instead of string concatenation.",
          "Avoid using JdbcTemplate.execute(String) with dynamically built SQL; use JdbcTemplate.query()/update() with parameter binding.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the parameter if it must be used, in addition to parameterization.",
          "Do not rely on output encoding (ESAPI encodeForHTML) as a substitute for SQL parameterization \u2014 it protects only against XSS in the response, not SQL injection."
        ]
      }
    },
