      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00040\") returned via SeparateClassRequest.getTheParameter (calls request.getParameter directly, no validation). This value flows into 'param' with only a null-check (defaulted to empty string), then directly into 'new java.io.File(param)' with no path normalization, whitelist check, or use of FilenameUtils.getName(). The resulting fileTarget is used in fileTarget.exists(), which performs a real filesystem check using the fully attacker-controlled path (including any '../' sequences). The only sanitizer applied (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied to fileTarget.toString() solely for the HTML output message, and does not affect the path used in the File constructor or the .exists() call. Thus the sink (File operations reflecting attacker path) is fed by unsanitized user input.",
