      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00044\") assigned to param (attacker-controlled HTTP parameter). This value is directly concatenated, unsanitized, into the LDAP filter string: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person)(uid=\" + param + \"))\". This filter is then passed directly to ctx.search(base, filter, sc) at line 59, the flagged LDAP query sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping parentheses, asterisks, backslashes, NUL) is applied to param before it is embedded in the filter. The only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later to output values (attr.get(), attr2.get(), and even the filter string itself when printed to the HTTP response) for HTML/XSS protection, not for LDAP filter escaping \u2014 it is applied on the output path, not on the input path feeding the search() call, and HTML encoding is not effective against LDAP metacharacters like '(' ')' '*' '\\0' anyway. Thus the injection point is unprotected.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping or use of a parameterized/safe filter-construction API, allowing attacker-controlled special characters (e.g., '*', ')', '(') to alter the filter logic.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the LDAP filter to bypass intended query logic, enumerate or retrieve unauthorized directory entries, or in some LDAP configurations modify search semantics, leading to information disclosure or unauthorized access to directory data.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use LDAP-safe encoding on all values inserted into filter strings (e.g., escape '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL per RFC 4515) before building the filter, such as via ESAPI's Encoder.encodeForLDAP() or a similar dedicated LDAP encoder.",
          "Prefer parameterized/typed LDAP query APIs (e.g., javax.naming.directory.DirContext search with filter arguments array) instead of manual string concatenation.",
          "Apply strict allow-list input validation on the parameter (e.g., restrict to expected uid character set) before using it in the filter.",
          "Ensure sanitization is applied at the point the tainted value is used to build the filter, not only when the result is later displayed to users."
        ]
      }
