          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled query parameter is decoded and written directly to response via format() without HTML escaping, enabling XSS.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.431
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() (attacker-controlled). The code extracts the substring after 'BenchmarkTest00047=' into `param`, then applies java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") \u2014 which only reverses URL percent-encoding and provides no HTML/XSS sanitization. This decoded, attacker-controlled `param` is then passed directly as the format string to response.getWriter().format(param, obj) at line 73, writing raw content to the HTTP response body without any HTML escaping. No validator, allow-list, or output encoder is applied anywhere on this path. An attacker can supply a query string like ?BenchmarkTest00047=<script>alert(1)</script> which, after URL-decoding, is written verbatim into the response, resulting in reflected XSS.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string data is decoded via URLDecoder (which does not perform HTML/JS escaping) and then written directly to the HTTP response writer via format(), bypassing any templating or output-encoding layer that would neutralize HTML/script content.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL whose query string is reflected unescaped into the HTTP response, allowing injection of arbitrary HTML/JavaScript that executes in the victim's browser in the context of the vulnerable site (reflected Cross-Site Scripting), enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or defacement.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the decoded parameter value before writing it to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or similar) before calling format()/println().",
          "Avoid using unvalidated/unencoded user input as a format string in String.format/Writer.format \u2014 treat it strictly as data, not a format specification.",
          "Prefer a templating engine (JSP/JSF, Thymeleaf, etc.) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the raw OutputStream/Writer.",
          "Set a strict Content-Security-Policy header to reduce impact of any residual injection.",
          "Validate/allow-list expected parameter values where possible instead of reflecting arbitrary user input."
        ]
      }
    },
