      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP cookie named 'BenchmarkTest00077' -> value URL-decoded into 'param'. Because guess=\"ABC\" and switchTarget=guess.charAt(2)=='C', the switch statement takes case 'C' and sets bar = param (fully attacker-controlled, no sanitization applied). bar is then concatenated into a command string: argList.add(\"echo \" + bar), and this list (\"sh\",\"-c\",\"echo \"+bar or cmd.exe /c ...) is passed to `new ProcessBuilder(argList)` and `pb.start()`. Since the entire 'echo <bar>' string is passed as a single argument to 'sh -c' / 'cmd.exe /c', the shell will interpret any shell metacharacters embedded in the cookie value, enabling OS command injection. No validation, allow-listing, or escaping of param/bar occurs anywhere in the flow before it reaches ProcessBuilder.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high"
      }
