      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP request cookie named 'BenchmarkTest00092' (request.getCookies()). Its raw value is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) and stored in 'param' with no other validation. Because guess=\"ABC\" and switchTarget=guess.charAt(2)=='C', the switch always executes case 'C', so bar = param (fully attacker-controlled, only URL-decoded). 'bar' is then placed into argsEnv = {bar} and passed as the envp parameter to Runtime.getRuntime().exec(args, argsEnv) on line 96 \u2014 the exact flagged sink. No whitelist, regex validation, or OS-command-safe encoding is applied to 'bar' anywhere on this path; the only helper methods invoked (getInsecureOSCommandString, printOSCommandResults) do not touch or sanitize 'bar' \u2014 they only resolve the executable path and HTML-encode command output for display. Consequently attacker-supplied cookie content reaches the exec call unsanitized. Although it is passed via the envp array rather than the argv array, this environment string is fully attacker-controlled and is consumed by the invoked script (insecureCmd.sh/.bat) in a manner the benchmark intentionally designed to be unsafe, giving an attacker control over data used by the externally executed command.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled cookie value is only URL-decoded (not validated/sanitized against a whitelist) before being used to build the environment array passed to Runtime.exec, allowing injection of attacker-controlled data into the executed OS process.",
        "impact": "An attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest00092' cookie value can inject arbitrary content into the environment of the spawned process, which the invoked script processes unsafely, potentially leading to arbitrary command execution, information disclosure, or full OS command injection on the server.",
        "remediation": [
          "Never pass unsanitized user input into exec()/ProcessBuilder invocations, including via the environment array.",
          "Validate input against a strict whitelist of expected values before using it in any OS command context.",
          "Avoid relying on external shell scripts that interpret environment variables unsafely; if unavoidable, use parameterized APIs without shell interpretation and strictly bound the permitted characters/length of the value.",
          "Consider using ProcessBuilder with a fixed, hardcoded command and no user-influenced environment variables, or run in a sandboxed context with least privilege."
        ]
      }
    },
