        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP cookie 'BenchmarkTest00112' value, retrieved via request.getCookies() and URL-decoded into 'param'. This flows unmodified through thing.doSomething(param) - both possible implementations (Thing1.doSomething returns input verbatim, Thing2.doSomething wraps in StringBuilder but performs no escaping/validation) - into 'bar'. 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')\". This string is passed to statement.executeUpdate(sql) with no parameterized query, prepared statement, or input sanitization/escaping applied anywhere on the path. A cookie value containing a single quote (e.g., ',(select ...),'--) would break out of the VALUES string literal and inject arbitrary SQL.",
