          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest00118.java:88:29-88:65:java.lang.security.audit.tainted-xpath-from-http-request.tainted-xpath-from-http-request",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "The variable 'bar' can receive attacker-controlled cookie input via URLDecoder.decode(), and although a conditional assigns a constant in the true branch, the else branch assigns the decoded cookie value directly into an XPath expression wi",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.9
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The cookie value is decoded into 'param' and then an if/else decides what 'bar' becomes. The condition is `(7 * 42) - num > 200` with num=86, i.e. `294 - 86 > 200` => `208 > 200`, which is always true. Therefore the if-branch always executes and bar is unconditionally set to the constant string \"This_should_always_happen\"; the else branch that assigns the tainted `param` (from the cookie) to `bar` is unreachable dead code. Since `bar` is always the hardcoded constant when it reaches `xp.evaluate(expression, xmlDocument)`, the XPath expression built from `bar` never contains attacker-controlled data in any real execution path.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high"
      }
    },
