          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest00146.java:59:9-59:67:java.lang.security.audit.xss.no-direct-response-writer.no-direct-response-writer",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled Referer header is URL-decoded and written directly to response.getWriter().format() without HTML escaping, enabling XSS despite minor string manipulation.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.464
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"Referer\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header) is read into `param`, URL-decoded, then copied into `bar`. Only the last character of `bar` is replaced with the literal 'Z' via StringBuilder.replace(); the rest of the attacker-supplied content (e.g. an injected <script> payload) is untouched. `bar` is then passed directly as the format string to response.getWriter().format(Locale.US, bar, obj), which writes the largely-unmodified attacker content straight to the raw response Writer. No HTML entity encoding, ESAPI encoder, or output sanitization is applied anywhere on this path, and writing via getWriter() bypasses any JSP/view-layer auto-escaping.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled Referer header value is decoded and echoed (nearly verbatim) into the HTTP response via a raw Writer without any HTML/JS output encoding or sanitization.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a request with a malicious Referer header (e.g., containing <script> tags) that gets reflected back into the HTML response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) that can lead to session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary JS execution in the victim's browser.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the Referer header value before writing it into the response (e.g., use OWASP ESAPI Encoder.encodeForHTML or a similar context-aware encoder).",
          "Avoid using untrusted input as a format string; treat it strictly as data.",
          "Prefer a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to response.getWriter().",
          "Validate/allow-list the Referer header format if it is used for display purposes."
        ]
      }
    },
