      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"Referer\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header) is read into 'param' at line 45. It is URL-decoded (line 49) preserving any encoded script payload, then wrapped in a StringBuilder and appended with the constant '_SafeStuff' (lines 51-52) producing 'bar', which still contains the raw attacker payload as a prefix. 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and passed to response.getWriter().printf(...) at line 56, writing it directly to the raw output stream. No HTML/JS output encoding, escaping, or validation is applied anywhere on this path (the '_SafeStuff' suffix is not a sanitizer, it just concatenates a trailing string). Because printf writes to the raw response writer instead of a template engine, any HTML/script content in the Referer header is reflected verbatim into the HTML response, resulting in classic reflected XSS.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled Referer header value is decoded and concatenated into a string that is written unescaped directly to the HTTP response via response.getWriter().printf(), bypassing any HTML-escaping view layer.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a Referer header (or induce a victim's browser/proxy to send one) containing malicious HTML/JavaScript that will be reflected in the response and executed in the victim's browser context, enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode/escape user-supplied data (Referer header value) before writing it into the response body, e.g., using OWASP Java Encoder (Encode.forHtml()) or a templating engine with auto-escaping.",
          "Avoid writing directly to response.getWriter()/OutputStream with untrusted data; use a view technology (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Set the 'X-XSS-Protection' header appropriately (do not disable it) and add a Content-Security-Policy header as defense in depth.",
          "Validate/allow-list expected format of the Referer header if it is used for business logic, rejecting or stripping unexpected characters."
        ]
      }
