        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP header 'BenchmarkTest00159' read via request.getHeader() at line ~44, then URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not perform any command sanitization. This value 'param' is passed to thing.doSomething(param) \u2014 both possible implementations (Thing1.doSomething just returns the input unchanged, Thing2.doSomething wraps it in a StringBuilder without any filtering) return the tainted value unmodified as 'bar'. 'bar' is then concatenated into a shell command string: args = {a1, a2, \"echo \" + bar}, where a1/a2 are 'sh'/'-c' or 'cmd.exe'/'/c'. This args array is passed directly to `new ProcessBuilder(args)` and `pb.start()` at line 67, meaning the tainted string is interpreted by a shell (-c flag), enabling injection of arbitrary shell metacharacters (e.g., ; | ` $() ) with no whitelist, escaping, or removal of shell metacharacters anywhere on the path.",
