      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest00191\") -> URL-decoded into 'param'. This taints 'param' in principle, but 'param' is only assigned to 'bar' in switch cases 'A', 'C', or 'D'. The switch variable 'switchTarget' is derived from a hardcoded local constant: String guess = \"ABC\"; switchTarget = guess.charAt(1), which is always 'B' (constant, not attacker-influenced). Consequently the switch statement always executes case 'B', setting bar = \"bob\" (a fixed literal), and the case 'A'/'C'/'D' branches that would assign the tainted param to bar are unreachable dead code. The SQL string 'sql = \"{call \" + bar + \"}\"' therefore always uses the constant \"bob\", never the tainted header value, before being passed to connection.prepareCall(sql, ...). Because the tainted value never reaches the sink through any live code path, the sink is effectively fed a constant.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The switch statement that would route tainted 'param' into the SQL-building variable 'bar' is guarded by a deterministic condition (switchTarget = \"ABC\".charAt(1) == 'B') that always selects the safe/default branch ('bob'), making the taint-carrying branches unreachable. The SAST tool performs simple data-flow reachability from source to sink without evaluating this constant-controlled branch condition, producing a false positive.",
        "impact": "None in current code as written; the SQL sink always executes with a constant value 'bob', not with attacker input. No SQL injection occurs through this specific execution path.",
        "remediation": [
          "No immediate action required since the tainted branch is unreachable, but remove dead/misleading code (the case 'A'/'C'/'D' -> bar = param branches) to avoid future refactoring accidentally activating the vulnerable path.",
          "If any future change makes 'guess' or 'switchTarget' derive from user input or configuration, use parameterized queries (PreparedStatement with bind variables) instead of string concatenation for the SQL command text.",
          "Add defensive input validation/allow-listing on the header value regardless, since it is user-controlled and URL-decoded before use."
        ]
      }
