        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the header value (e.g., using a single quote to break out of the PASSWORD literal), potentially bypassing authentication logic, extracting or modifying data, or in some database configurations executing further malicious SQL commands.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries / PreparedStatement (or Spring JdbcTemplate's parameterized update methods) instead of concatenating user input into SQL strings.",
