        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest00198\") is attacker-controlled HTTP header. It's URL-decoded then passed to thing.doSomething(param). Both possible ThingInterface implementations shown (Thing1.doSomething, Thing2.doSomething) return the input unchanged/copied with no sanitization or escaping. The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"... PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" and executed via DatabaseHelper.JDBCtemplate.queryForObject(sql, Integer.class) \u2014 a raw SQL string execution, not a parameterized query. No validation, allow-listing, or SQL escaping occurs anywhere on this path before the sink. The ESAPI encodeForHTML call only occurs in an exception handler for HTML output of the sql string, not as a sanitizer before the query executes.",
