          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled HTTP header is URL-decoded and Base64-encoded but not sanitized before being concatenated into an XPath expression string, enabling XPath injection attacks.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.469
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest00207\") (line ~44) is attacker-controlled. It's URL-decoded and assigned to param, then run through Base64.encodeBase64 followed by decodeBase64 producing bar - a no-op round trip that returns the same bytes as param, so bar == param (no sanitization occurs). bar is then concatenated directly into an XPath expression string: \"/Employees/Employee[@emplid='\" + bar + \"']\" (line 75) and passed to xp.evaluate(expression, xmlDocument), the flagged sink. There is no escaping of XPath meta-characters (e.g. single quotes) before this concatenation, so an attacker can inject payloads like ' or '1'='1 to alter the XPath query and potentially exfiltrate arbitrary XML data. The only encoding present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later, only in the exception handler for HTML output, and does not sanitize the XPath expression before evaluate() is called.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header value is decoded and passed through a no-op Base64 encode/decode round trip (which does not sanitize anything) and then concatenated directly into an XPath expression string without escaping XPath special characters, before being passed to XPath.evaluate().",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the XPath query logic (XPath injection) to bypass intended query constraints, potentially extracting arbitrary data from the XML document (e.g., all employee records) or altering query semantics, leading to unauthorized information disclosure.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized XPath queries via XPathVariableResolver instead of string concatenation.",
          "Strictly validate/whitelist the input format expected for emplid (e.g., numeric-only) before use.",
          "Escape XPath special characters (particularly single quotes) in user input before embedding it into an XPath expression.",
          "Do not rely on Base64 encode/decode as a sanitization mechanism since it is reversible and preserves the original content."
        ]
      }
    },
