          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled Referer header is decoded and written directly to response via getWriter().print() without HTML escaping, enabling XSS.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.504
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") is attacker-controlled (any client can set arbitrary Referer header value). It's assigned to `param`, then URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode (which does not perform HTML/JS escaping, only URL decoding). The ternary condition `(7*42)-num>200` evaluates to `294-106=188>200` which is false, so `bar` is always assigned `param` (the raw decoded header value). This value flows directly to `response.getWriter().print(bar)` with no HTML escaping, no output encoding, and no allowlist/denylist validation applied anywhere on the path. This is a direct sink write of tainted data.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP Referer header value is decoded and printed directly to the response writer without any HTML/JS output encoding or sanitization, allowing injection of arbitrary script content into the HTML response.",
        "impact": "An attacker who can influence the Referer header (e.g., via a crafted link, malicious referring page, or intercepting proxy) can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript that executes in the victim's browser in the context of the vulnerable site, leading to reflected XSS: session hijacking, credential theft, defacement, or further client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the value before writing to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or similar) instead of raw print().",
          "Avoid writing directly to the raw OutputStream/Writer for user-influenced content; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF/Thymeleaf) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Do not trust the Referer header for reflecting content back to the user; if it must be displayed, treat it as untrusted input and encode/sanitize appropriately for the output context (HTML body, attribute, JS, etc.).",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
    },
