      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00295\") reads an attacker-controlled HTTP header value into 'param'. It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) but not sanitized against shell metacharacters. The ternary 'bar = (7*42)-num>200 ? ... : param' evaluates the numeric condition (294-106=188>200 \u2192 false) so bar is always assigned the raw decoded header value. This is concatenated into args[2] = \"echo \" + bar, which is passed to 'new ProcessBuilder(args)' and executed via pb.start(). No validation, allow-listing, or shell-metacharacter escaping is applied to bar before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink. The downstream Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the command's stdout/stderr for display, which is irrelevant to preventing injection into the command itself.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP header value is decoded and passed unsanitized into a shell command executed via ProcessBuilder(\"sh\",\"-c\",\"echo \"+bar), allowing shell metacharacters (e.g., ; | & `) to inject additional commands.",
        "impact": "An attacker who can control the 'BenchmarkTest00295' HTTP header can inject arbitrary OS commands executed with the privileges of the web application process, leading to remote code execution, data exfiltration, or full system compromise.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (\"sh -c\"/\"cmd /c\") with concatenated user input; instead pass command and arguments as separate array elements without a shell wrapper.",
          "Strictly validate/allow-list the header value (e.g., only alphanumeric characters) before using it in any command.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed command and pass user data only as a discrete argument, never concatenated into a shell string.",
          "Consider using established libraries or APIs that avoid shell invocation entirely for the intended functionality."
        ]
      }
    },
