      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source is request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00323\") -> param (attacker-controlled, URL-decoded). However param is only assigned to 'bar' in the else-branch of `if ((7*42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;`. With num=86, (7*42)-86 = 294-86 = 208, and 208 > 200 evaluates to true at compile/runtime for all inputs, so the if-branch always executes and bar is always assigned the constant string \"This_should_always_happen\". The else branch (bar = param) is dead code and never executed. Therefore request.getSession().putValue(\"userid\", bar) at line 61 always stores a hardcoded constant, never the tainted param value.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The tainted value is only assigned to the sink-bound variable in an unreachable else branch; the if-condition is a constant expression that always evaluates true, so the tainted branch never executes and the sink always receives a hardcoded string.",
        "impact": "None in current form since the sink only ever receives a constant value; no attacker-controlled data reaches the session store.",
        "remediation": [
          "Remove the dead/never-taken branch and confirm actual data flow reaching session storage.",
          "If real user input is intended to reach the session, treat it as trust-boundary sensitive: validate/allow-list before storing in HttpSession, and re-validate on read.",
          "Ensure test/benchmark logic reflects genuine conditional branching so static analysis and manual review are not misled by dead code."
        ]
      }
    },
