        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00325\") returns attacker-controlled HTTP header values. The first header value is extracted (headers.nextElement()), URL-decoded, then passed through StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml() (an HTML-output encoder) and stored via request.getSession().putValue(\"userid\", bar). escapeHtml sanitizes for HTML-context XSS but does nothing to address CWE-501 Trust Boundary Violation, which concerns storing externally-controlled data directly into session state without any boundary-crossing validation/reclassification. No validation of the header content (e.g., allow-listing expected user IDs) occurs before it is persisted in the session object under a trusted-sounding key ('userid').",
