      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source is request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00336\") -> param, URL-decoded, then flows to 'bar' only in the else branch of `if ((7*42)-num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;`. Evaluating the constant expression: 7*42=294, 294-86=208, and 208>200 is always true, so the if-branch always executes and bar is always assigned the fixed literal \"This_should_always_happen\". The else branch (bar = param, tainted) is dead code and can never execute. Consequently the SQL string `sql = \"...PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\"` used in queryForObject is always built from a constant, never from user input, so no attacker-controlled data reaches the SQL sink.",
