        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The branch that would assign the tainted HTTP header value to 'bar' is unreachable due to a constant conditional expression that always evaluates to true, causing 'bar' to always be set to a hardcoded string instead of the tainted param.",
        "impact": "None in current code path since the tainted value never reaches the SQL sink; however if the constant condition were changed or removed, tainted data would flow directly into a raw SQL string.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries (PreparedStatement) instead of string concatenation regardless of the current dead branch, to prevent future SQL injection if the constant condition changes.",
          "Remove or fix the always-true conditional so behavior is unambiguous and add explicit input validation/allow-listing on the header value.",
          "Add unit tests to guard against reintroducing tainted data into raw SQL construction."
        ]
      }
