      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest00344\") -> param -> URL-decoded. However bar is only assigned param in the else branch of `if ((7*42)-num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;`. Evaluating the condition: (7*42)-86 = 294-86 = 208, and 208>200 is always true, so the if-branch is always taken and bar is always the hardcoded constant \"This_should_always_happen\". The else branch that assigns tainted param to bar is dead code and never executes. Consequently the SQL string concatenation `... PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\"` never contains attacker input, so the flagged sink at line 65 never receives tainted data.",
