        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated into a file path without any path traversal sanitization (e.g., no use of FilenameUtils.getName, canonical path checks, or whitelist validation) before being used to construct a File/FileOutputStream.",
        "impact": "An attacker can write arbitrary files outside the intended directory (path traversal / arbitrary file write), potentially overwriting critical files, planting malicious files (e.g., web shells), or causing denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use FilenameUtils.getName() or similar to strip any directory components from the user-supplied parameter before use.",
          "Validate the resulting file name against a strict whitelist (e.g., alphanumeric only).",
          "After constructing the File, resolve its canonical path and verify it still resides within the intended base directory before performing any file operations.",
          "Avoid directly concatenating user input into file paths; instead map input to pre-defined safe file identifiers."
        ]
      }
    },
