      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00363\") is assigned to 'param' (or empty string if null), then copied to 'bar', then concatenated with Utils.TESTFILES_DIR to build 'fileName' with no path normalization or validation. This fileName is passed directly into 'new java.io.FileInputStream(fileName)' at line 60, the flagged sink. The only sanitizer present, ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(fileName), is applied afterward and only to the value written to the HTTP response body \u2014 it does not affect or sanitize the fileName used to open the FileInputStream. No path canonicalization (e.g., getCanonicalPath + prefix check) or FilenameUtils.getName() call is applied to the user-controlled 'bar' before it is used in the file path. An attacker can supply a value like '../../../../etc/passwd' or an absolute path via the BenchmarkTest00363 parameter to escape the TESTFILES_DIR directory and open an arbitrary file on the filesystem.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high"
      }
