        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00378\") is read into 'param' (line 43). It is concatenated via StringBuilder with a constant suffix '_SafeStuff' to form 'bar' (lines 46-47) \u2014 no HTML encoding or sanitization occurs at this step. 'bar' is then passed directly as the format string to response.getWriter().format(bar, obj) (line 51), which writes the resulting text directly to the HTTP response's OutputStream/Writer without going through any templating/encoding layer. Since 'bar' contains raw attacker input (plus a fixed suffix), an attacker can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript (e.g., '<script>alert(1)</script>_SafeStuff') which will be echoed verbatim into the response body, since the format string itself contains no '%' specifiers to consume the 'obj' array in a way that would strip attacker content. No output encoder or input validator is applied anywhere on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied request parameter is incorporated into a string that is written directly to the response writer via format() without any HTML/JS output encoding, bypassing template-based auto-escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a malicious parameter value containing HTML/JavaScript that will be reflected unescaped in the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary actions in the victim's browser context.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the parameter value before including it in any output written to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Avoid writing raw, user-controlled strings directly via response.getWriter(); use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that automatically escapes output.",
          "If format() must be used, treat all user input strictly as format arguments (data), never as part of the format string itself.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense-in-depth."
        ]
      }
