        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00388\") assigned to 'param' (line 43). It is appended unmodified to a StringBuilder and concatenated with a constant suffix '_SafeStuff' (line 46-47), producing 'bar'. This value is then written directly to the HTTP response via response.getWriter().println(bar.toCharArray()) (line 50) with no HTML/JS encoding, escaping, or validation applied anywhere on the path. The only header set is X-XSS-Protection: 0, which actually disables the browser's built-in XSS auditor rather than mitigating the issue. Since the parameter value is reflected verbatim into the response body, an attacker can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript via the 'BenchmarkTest00388' request parameter, resulting in reflected XSS.",
