          "reason": "User input from request parameter is Base64-encoded then decoded (no sanitization) and written directly to response writer, allowing XSS injection.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.332
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00390\") assigned to param (attacker-controlled). param is Base64-encoded then immediately Base64-decoded via org.apache.commons.codec.binary.Base64.decodeBase64(encodeBase64(param.getBytes())) which is a no-op round trip that returns the original bytes unchanged - it is not a sanitizer, merely obfuscation. The result 'bar' equals the original user input. This value is then written directly to the response via response.getWriter().println(bar) at line 56, with no HTML-encoding, escaping, or output-encoding library applied anywhere on the path. The X-XSS-Protection header is even explicitly disabled (set to \"0\"), removing a browser-side mitigation. This is a direct reflected XSS sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied request parameter is written to the HTTP response body via the raw Writer without any HTML/JS output encoding or validation; the Base64 encode/decode round-trip provides no actual sanitization since it reconstructs the original input bytes exactly.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script in the BenchmarkTest00390 parameter (e.g. <script>alert(1)</script>) that will be reflected unescaped into the HTML response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting, allowing session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary actions in the victim's browser context.",
        "remediation": [
          "Encode output using a context-aware encoder (e.g. OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) before writing to the response.",
          "Use a view/templating technology (JSP/JSF/Thymeleaf) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the raw Writer/OutputStream.",
          "Validate/allow-list the parameter value if only specific characters are expected.",
          "Re-enable and rely on the browser XSS auditor by not overriding X-XSS-Protection to 0, and add a strict Content-Security-Policy header as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
    },
