        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00395\") assigned to param (line 43). param is split on space and first token stored in bar (line 47) - split() performs no HTML encoding/escaping, it merely tokenizes the string, so a payload like '<script>alert(1)</script>' (no spaces) passes through unchanged as bar. bar is then written directly to the response writer via response.getWriter().write(bar, 0, length) (line 53), which is a raw OutputStream/Writer sink that performs no HTML entity encoding. There is no validator, allow-list check, or encoder (e.g. ESAPI encoder, StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml) anywhere on this path. Content-Type is text/html, so any HTML/JS in bar is rendered by the browser as markup, and X-XSS-Protection is explicitly disabled making browser XSS filters ineffective. This is a direct, unsanitized reflected XSS.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP request parameter is reflected into the HTTP response body via a raw Writer.write() call without any HTML/JS output encoding or sanitization, and the split(' ')[0] operation does not neutralize HTML/script content.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script in the BenchmarkTest00395 parameter (with no spaces) that will be reflected verbatim into the page and executed in the victim's browser, enabling reflected cross-site scripting: session hijacking, credential theft, defacement, or further client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "Encode output using a context-aware HTML encoder (e.g., OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) before writing user input to the response.",
          "Use a view/templating technology (JSP/JSF/Thymeleaf) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the response Writer.",
          "Validate/allow-list the parameter value against expected format if it should not contain HTML/script content.",
          "Re-enable or rely on framework-level XSS protections rather than disabling X-XSS-Protection header."
        ]
      }
    },
