        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest00436\") assigned to `param`. However, `bar` (which flows into the SQL string concatenation `... PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'`) is only assigned `param` in the else-branch of `if ((7 * 42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;`. Evaluating the condition: (7*42) - 86 = 294 - 86 = 208, and 208 > 200 is always true. This means the if-branch is always taken and `bar` is always set to the hardcoded constant \"This_should_always_happen\"; the else-branch containing the tainted `param` is dead code that can never execute. Consequently the tainted HTTP parameter never reaches the `sql` string or the `statement.execute(sql)` sink.",
