        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the BenchmarkTest00438 parameter (e.g., using a payload like ' OR '1'='1) to bypass authentication logic, extract or modify data, or in some DB configurations execute further malicious SQL commands.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use java.sql.PreparedStatement with parameterized placeholders (?) instead of string concatenation.",
          "Bind the user-supplied value via setString() rather than embedding it directly in the SQL text.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the parameter as defense in depth.",
          "Avoid Statement.execute() with dynamically built SQL strings."
        ]
      }
