        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied request parameter is concatenated into a file path used to construct a java.io.File without any path traversal sanitization; the Base64 encode/decode round-trip is a no-op and does not filter '../' sequences.",
        "impact": "An attacker can use path traversal sequences to probe the filesystem for the existence of arbitrary files outside the intended directory (information disclosure of file system layout), and depending on downstream use of fileTarget, could enable further file-based attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "Canonicalize the resulting File path (getCanonicalPath()) and verify it still resides within the intended base directory (TESTFILES_DIR) before using it.",
          "Reject or strip '../' and other path traversal sequences from user input using an allow-list of expected filenames.",
          "Use FilenameUtils.getName(...) or similar utility to extract only the file name component from user input, discarding any directory traversal segments.",
          "Avoid constructing file paths directly from user input; instead map user input to a fixed set of allowed files via an indirect lookup (e.g., a whitelist map)."
        ]
      }
