        "exploitability_evidence": "The tainted source is request.getParameterMap() -> param, assigned to bar only in the else branch of `if ((7 * 42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;`. Evaluating the constant expression: (7*42)-num = 294-86 = 208, and 208 > 200 is always true, so the if-branch is always taken and bar is always set to the hardcoded string \"This_should_always_happen\". The else branch (bar = param, the tainted user input) is dead code and can never execute. Consequently fileName = TESTFILES_DIR + bar always uses the constant value, never attacker-controlled input, so the FileInputStream sink at line 62 never receives tainted data.",
