        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() -> param (attacker-controlled). This value is only assigned to 'bar' in switch cases 'A', 'C', or 'D'. However, switchTarget is derived from a hardcoded constant string \"ABC\".charAt(1), which always evaluates to 'B'. The switch statement therefore always executes case 'B', setting bar = \"bob\" (a hardcoded literal), and the branches that would assign the tainted param to bar are dead code, never reached at runtime. Consequently fileName = TESTFILES_DIR + \"bob\" is always a fixed, non-attacker-controlled path passed to new File(fileName) and FileOutputStream. The tainted param never reaches the sink.",
