      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() -> param (line 43-47) is attacker-controlled via the 'BenchmarkTest00492' request parameter. It flows unmodified into thing.doSomething(param). Both possible implementations (Thing1.doSomething and Thing2.doSomething, the only ones shown, selected via ThingFactory.createThing) simply return the input string unchanged (Thing1: 'String r = i; return r;', Thing2: 'new StringBuilder(i).toString()'). The returned value 'bar' is then concatenated into a string and written directly to the response writer via response.getWriter().write(\"Parameter value: \" + bar) with no HTML-encoding, escaping, or output-encoding library applied anywhere on the path. This is a direct write to OutputStream/Writer bypassing any templating/auto-escaping, matching the CWE-79 sink pattern exactly.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is passed through pass-through helper methods (Thing1/Thing2.doSomething) that perform no sanitization or encoding, and the result is written directly to the HTTP response body without HTML escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script in the 'BenchmarkTest00492' parameter (e.g. <script>alert(1)</script>) which will be reflected verbatim in the HTML response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS). This can lead to session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary actions performed in the victim's browser session.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the 'bar' value before writing it into the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or similar context-aware encoding).",
          "Prefer a templating engine (JSP/JSF, Thymeleaf, etc.) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the raw Writer/OutputStream.",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected format of the parameter if it should only contain specific characters (e.g., alphanumeric).",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
    },
