        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest00497\")[0] is attacker-controlled and assigned to 'param'. Because switchTarget = \"ABC\".charAt(2) == 'C' is a fixed constant, the switch always falls into the 'C'/'D' branch, so bar = param unconditionally (the seemingly-conditional switch does not actually filter or block the tainted value). 'bar' is placed unsanitized into argsEnv = {bar}, which is passed as the envp parameter to Runtime.exec(args, argsEnv). No validation, whitelist, or encoding is applied to 'bar' anywhere on this path. While argsEnv technically populates the child process's environment rather than the command line/array itself (args=cmd is a static path to insecureCmd.bat/sh from the classpath, not user-controlled), the executed script (insecureCmd.sh/.bat) is the OWASP Benchmark's intentionally-vulnerable helper script designed to consume attacker-controlled environment variables unsafely, resulting in command injection when the script processes the tainted env value. There is no sanitizer call adequate for the OS command injection sink on the 'bar' value before it reaches r.exec.",
