      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: `param` is read directly from `request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest00499\")` (attacker-controlled HTTP parameter). It flows unmodified into `bar = param`, then into `r.exec(cmd + bar, argsEnv)` at line 62, which is the flagged sink. `cmd` is either empty string or 'cmd.exe /c echo ' (via Utils.getOSCommandString), so the final executed string is 'cmd.exe /c echo ' + bar on Windows (interpreted by the Windows shell, allowing '&', '|', etc. to chain commands) or just bar on other OSes (executed as an arbitrary program/args via Runtime.exec tokenization). No validation, whitelist, or escaping is applied to `param`/`bar` anywhere on this path \u2014 Utils.getOSCommandString only prepends a fixed prefix and does not sanitize; Utils.printOSCommandResults only handles output encoding for the HTML response, not command sanitization. Therefore user input reaches the OS command execution sink unsanitized.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into a string passed to Runtime.exec() without any validation, escaping, or whitelisting of allowed values.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject OS command syntax (e.g., '&', '|', ';' on Windows via cmd.exe /c) to execute arbitrary commands on the host system, potentially leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking OS commands with user-supplied input; use Java APIs instead of shelling out where possible.",
          "If exec is unavoidable, use Runtime.exec(String[]) with a fixed command and pass user input only as a strictly validated argument (e.g., against a whitelist of allowed characters/values).",
          "Do not use 'cmd.exe /c' or any shell invocation with concatenated user input, as it enables shell metacharacter injection.",
          "Validate and canonicalize the parameter value against an allow-list before use, rejecting any input containing shell metacharacters."
        ]
      }
