        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() extracts values for key 'BenchmarkTest00510' into 'param' (attacker-controlled via HTTP request parameter). Since guess=\"ABC\" is a constant, switchTarget = guess.charAt(2) = 'C' is always true, so the switch statement deterministically executes case 'C', assigning bar = param (unsanitized user input). This bar is directly concatenated into the SQL string: sql = \"{call \" + bar + \"}\". This tainted sql string is passed unmodified to connection.prepareCall(sql, ...) which is executed via statement.executeQuery(). No sanitizer, encoder, or parameterization is applied to 'bar' or 'sql' anywhere on this path \u2014 the DatabaseHelper methods (getSqlConnection, printResults) only handle connection setup and HTML-encoding of query results, not SQL input sanitization. This is a textbook SQL injection via string concatenation into a CallableStatement.",
