        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest00512\") returns attacker-controlled array; values[0] is assigned to param, then to bar. bar is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" with no escaping, encoding, or parameterization. This raw string sql is passed to statement.execute(sql) where statement is a java.sql.Statement (not PreparedStatement) obtained from DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement(). No sanitizer or validator is applied to bar/param anywhere on this path before it reaches the SQL execution sink. The only encoding present in the code (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied later in printResults for HTML output rendering, not for SQL sanitization, so it does not mitigate this sink.",
