          "HTML-encode/escape the value before writing it to the response (e.g. use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or similar) instead of writing raw user-derived data via getWriter().println().",
          "Use a templating/view technology (JSP with auto-escaping, JSF, Thymeleaf) that automatically escapes output rather than writing directly to the raw OutputStream/Writer.",
          "Avoid reflecting untrusted parameter names/values back to the client at all where not strictly necessary; validate/allow-list expected parameter names.",
          "Re-enable/restore browser XSS protections (do not explicitly disable X-XSS-Protection) as defense-in-depth, though primary fix is proper output encoding."
        ]
