      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The sink is r.exec(args, argsEnv, ...) at line ~74, where args=[cmd] (a fixed path to insecureCmd.sh/bat from classpath, not user-controlled) and argsEnv=[bar]. bar is intended to be user-controlled via 'param' (derived from an HTTP parameter name), but the assignment is guarded by 'if ((7 * 42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;' with num=86. Evaluating: 7*42=294, 294-86=208, and 208>200 is always true. Therefore the if-branch is always taken and bar is always set to the hardcoded string \"This_should_always_happen\" \u2014 the else branch assigning the tainted 'param' value is dead code and can never execute. Consequently no attacker-controlled data ever reaches the ProcessBuilder/exec sink; both cmd and argsEnv are effectively constant at runtime.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The branch condition '(7 * 42) - num > 200' with num=86 evaluates to 208 > 200, which is always true, so the code path that would assign the tainted HTTP-derived 'param' value to 'bar' is unreachable dead code. The value actually used in the exec call is a hardcoded constant.",
        "impact": "No security impact in the current code as written since attacker-controlled data never reaches the OS command execution sink. If the arithmetic constants were ever changed such that the else branch becomes reachable, tainted parameter names would flow into environment variables passed to exec, enabling command/environment injection.",
        "remediation": [
          "Even though currently unreachable, remove or fix the dead code path so it does not silently mask a latent vulnerability.",
          "If user input must influence command execution, validate it against a strict whitelist of expected values before use.",
          "Avoid passing user-influenced data as environment variables or arguments to exec/ProcessBuilder; use parutTerized APIs and restrict process execution to fixed, non-configurable commands.",
          "Add unit/integration tests to confirm which branch is actually taken to prevent accidental reactivation of the vulnerable path."
        ]
      }
    },
