      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP parameter names from request.getParameterNames(); the code iterates parameter names and picks the first parameter name whose value equals the literal 'BenchmarkTest00603'. Since an attacker fully controls both parameter names and values, they can set an arbitrary parameter name (e.g. a SQL injection payload) with a value equal to 'BenchmarkTest00603', causing param to become the attacker-chosen name string. This value flows to thing.doSomething(param) \u2014 both Thing1.doSomething and Thing2.doSomething return the input unmodified (identity pass-through, no sanitization). The result (bar) is directly concatenated into the SQL string: 'SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='' + bar + ''\"'. This concatenated string is then passed to statement.execute(sql, ...) with no parameterization or escaping. No sanitizer, validator, or prepared statement is present on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled input (HTTP parameter name) is passed through an identity transformation and concatenated directly into a SQL query string, which is then executed via Statement.execute() instead of a parameterized PreparedStatement.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL syntax into the WHERE clause, potentially bypassing authentication, extracting or modifying arbitrary data in the USERS table, or performing further SQL injection attacks (union-based extraction, blind boolean/time-based injection, etc.), depending on the underlying database and permissions.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a parameterized PreparedStatement with bind variables instead of string concatenation for the SQL query.",
          "Never build SQL queries from raw HTTP parameter names or values without strict allow-list validation.",
          "Apply input validation/allow-listing on parameter names/values before using them in any downstream operation, especially SQL.",
          "Enable least-privilege database accounts to limit the impact of a successful injection."
        ]
      }
