      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The tainted value 'param' is derived from request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() when a parameter value equals 'BenchmarkTest00605', in which case 'param' is set to the parameter name (attacker-controlled). This flows into bar = (7*18)+num > 200 ? \"This_should_always_happen\" : param; . The condition (7*18)+num > 200 evaluates to 126+106=232 > 200, which is always true (num is a hardcoded constant 106). Therefore bar is always assigned the constant string \"This_should_always_happen\" and the tainted 'param' branch is dead code, never executed. The resulting sql string used in statement.executeUpdate(sql) is always the fixed string \"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','This_should_always_happen')\" with no attacker-controlled data reaching the SQL sink.",
