        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "info",
        "root_cause": "The ternary condition controlling which value (constant vs. tainted param) is assigned to 'bar' is a compile-time-constant-evaluable expression that is always true, making the tainted branch unreachable dead code. The SAST tool's taint tracker does not evaluate the always-true condition and flags the theoretical tainted path even though it can never execute.",
        "impact": "None \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the SQL statement executed always contains only constant, hardcoded values; no user input reaches the SQL sink in practice.",
        "remediation": [
          "No fix required for this specific instance since the vulnerable branch is unreachable, but consider using parameterized queries/PreparedStatement universally as a best practice.",
          "If the ternary logic is intended to sometimes use user input, ensure the tainted branch would use a PreparedStatement with bound parameters instead of string concatenation."
        ]
