          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User input from request parameter is directly written to response writer without any sanitization or encoding, enabling XSS.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.62
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00715\") returns user-controlled input, assigned to param. param is split on space delimiter (bar = param.split(\" \")[0]) which does not perform any HTML/JS encoding or sanitization - it merely tokenizes the string, preserving any XSS payload placed before the first space (e.g., '<script>alert(1)</script>'). bar is then written directly to the response writer via response.getWriter().print(bar) with Content-Type text/html, with no output encoding applied. The X-XSS-Protection header is also explicitly disabled ('0'), removing browser-side mitigation. No sanitizer/encoder is present on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Unsanitized, attacker-controlled HTTP parameter is written directly to the HTTP response body without HTML-encoding or use of a templating/view layer that would auto-escape it.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script in the BenchmarkTest00715 parameter (e.g., a payload without spaces to avoid truncation from split) that gets reflected into the response and executed in the victim's browser, enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the value before writing it to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the raw Writer/OutputStream.",
          "Validate/whitelist expected input format for the parameter.",
          "Re-enable and rely on additional defenses like Content-Security-Policy headers instead of disabling X-XSS-Protection."
        ]
      }
    },
