      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00719\") user input assigned to param. It is passed to thing.doSomething(param) where thing is created via ThingFactory.createThing(); both possible implementations shown (Thing1.doSomething and Thing2.doSomething) return the input unchanged (pass-through, no encoding/escaping). The returned value 'bar' is then used directly as the format string in response.getWriter().printf(Locale.US, bar, obj) at line 54. This writes attacker-controlled content directly to the HTTP response via the raw Writer, bypassing any HTML-escaping view layer. No sanitizer, encoder, or validator is applied anywhere on this path.",
