        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied request parameter is passed unmodified through a pass-through helper method and used as the format argument to Writer.printf(), which writes it directly into the HTTP response without HTML/context-aware output encoding.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject HTML/JavaScript via the request parameter, which is reflected unescaped in the response body, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) that can lead to session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode/escape user input before writing it to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Avoid using untrusted input directly as a format string; treat it strictly as data, not as the format specifier.",
          "Use a templating/view technology (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output instead of writing directly to the raw response Writer.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
