        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00723\") assigned to 'param'. This flows to 'bar' only in the else branch of 'if ((7 * 42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;'. Evaluating the condition: 7*42=294, num=86, 294-86=208, and 208>200 is always true. Therefore the if-branch always executes, bar is always assigned the constant \"This_should_always_happen\", and the else branch that assigns the tainted 'param' to 'bar' is dead code that can never execute at runtime. The sink response.getWriter().printf(bar, obj) therefore never receives attacker-controlled data \u2014 bar is always the hardcoded string.",
