      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00731\") -> assigned to param -> bar (no validation/sanitization). bar is concatenated into a single list element \"echo \" + bar which is added to argList after [\"sh\",\"-c\"] (or [\"cmd.exe\",\"/c\"] on Windows). This argList is passed to new ProcessBuilder(argList) and pb.start() is invoked at line 60. Because the command is executed via a shell (-c flag), the shell parses the whole string, so any shell metacharacters in bar (e.g. ; | ` $() ) are interpreted by the shell rather than treated as literal data. There is no whitelist, escaping, or use of ProcessBuilder in a form that treats bar as a single literal argument (it's embedded inside a shell command string). The only downstream processing (Utils.printOSCommandResults) HTML-encodes command output for the response, which does not mitigate the injection into the shell command itself.",
