        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00731\") assigns to param, then bar = param (unsanitized). This value flows into argList.add(\"echo \" + bar), which is passed to `sh -c` (or `cmd.exe /c` on Windows) via `new ProcessBuilder(argList)` and pb.start(). Because the command is invoked with a shell (-c flag), any shell metacharacters in bar (e.g. ; | & $() backticks) will be interpreted by the shell, allowing arbitrary command injection. No sanitization, allow-listing, or escaping is applied to bar before it is concatenated into the shell command line. The only downstream processing (Utils.printOSCommandResults) applies ESAPI HTML-encoding to the process's stdout/stderr for safe HTML rendering \u2014 this occurs after command execution and has no bearing on preventing the injection into the shell.",
