      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The tainted source is request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00763\") assigned to param, then param is only assigned to bar inside switch cases 'A', 'C', 'D'. However switchTarget = guess.charAt(1) where guess is the constant string \"ABC\", so switchTarget is always the character 'B' (index 1). Since 'B' matches the case that assigns bar = \"bob\" (a hardcoded literal), the branches assigning bar = param ('A','C','D') are unreachable dead code. Consequently the sql string concatenation '...PASSWORD='' + bar + '''' always uses the constant \"bob\", never user input, before being passed to connection.prepareStatement. The tainted param never actually reaches the SQL sink at runtime.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The switch statement's controlling value is derived from a hardcoded constant string ('ABC'.charAt(1) == 'B'), making the branches that would assign user-controlled input to the SQL-bound variable unreachable dead code. The SAST tool's dataflow analysis flags the syntactic assignment param -> bar without recognizing that the switch condition is a compile-time constant that always selects the safe branch.",
        "impact": "None in the current code path \u2014 the SQL statement always uses the constant literal 'bob' as the password value, so no injection is possible via this endpoint. If the constant guess were ever changed to include user input, or if switchTarget's determination changed, this could become exploitable, but as written it is not.",
        "remediation": [
          "No immediate action required since the vulnerable branch is unreachable in this test case; if this pattern exists in production code, remove dead/unreachable branches or ensure they cannot be reintroduced",
          "As a general best practice, use PreparedStatement placeholders (?) for all variable SQL literals rather than string concatenation, even for values that appear currently unreachable, to prevent future regressions",
          "Add unit tests or static assertions to guarantee that guess/switchTarget cannot be influenced by external input if this pattern is intentional for testing"
        ]
      }
    },
