      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Sink at line 76: response.getWriter().println(\"Your results are: \" + String.valueOf(results)). 'results' is declared as Long and is the return value of JDBCtemplate.queryForObject(sql, Long.class) - i.e., a numeric userid column value from the DB, not raw attacker-supplied text. Although the SQL string itself is built by concatenating the unsanitized 'param' (from request.getParameterValues) into a query (a genuine SQL injection risk, CWE-89), that concatenated string is never written back to the response on this line - only the numeric Long result is. Since a Long cannot carry HTML/script markup, there is no attacker-controlled markup reaching the writer at this sink, so no XSS is achievable via this code path. The other catch branches that do echo attacker-influenced content (the SQL string) explicitly use ESAPI's encodeForHTML before writing, showing appropriate encoding is applied when raw string content is reflected.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The scanner flagged a generic getWriter().println sink pattern but the actual value written at line 76 (String.valueOf(results)) is derived from a Long database column value, not from unsanitized user input reflected as text; thus no attacker-controlled markup can reach the HTTP response at this specific sink.",
        "impact": "No XSS impact via this sink since the output is strictly numeric. (Note: a separate SQL Injection vulnerability exists due to unsanitized concatenation of 'param' into the SQL query, but that is outside the scope of this XSS finding.)",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries/prepared statements for the SQL string to address the underlying SQL injection issue.",
          "If future changes cause raw string data (e.g., the SQL text or user input) to be written to the response, ensure it is HTML-encoded (e.g., via ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) as already done in the exception-handling branches.",
          "Consider using a templating engine that auto-escapes output to reduce reliance on manual encoding decisions."
        ]
      }
