        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest00768\") assigns attacker-controlled value to param. This flows unmodified into thing.doSomething(param) \u2014 both Thing1.doSomething and Thing2.doSomething shown here simply return the input string as-is (Thing1: 'String r = i; return r;'; Thing2: wraps in StringBuilder but no encoding/escaping). The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"...PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\", forming variable 'sql'. This sql string is passed as-is to DatabaseHelper.JDBCtemplate.queryForMap(sql), which executes it as raw SQL (no PreparedStatement/parameter binding). No sanitizer, escaper, or allow-list validation is applied to param/bar anywhere on this path \u2014 the ESAPI encodeForHTML calls only occur on already-executed query results or the sql string in an error message, not before use in the query. Therefore attacker input reaches the SQL sink unsanitized.",
