        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> extracted substring 'param' -> URLDecoder.decode(param, 'UTF-8'). guess='ABC', switchTarget=guess.charAt(2)='C', so the switch statement executes case 'C': bar = param (attacker-controlled, decoded value). This bar is placed into obj array and written via response.getWriter().format(\"Formatted like: %1$s and %2$s.\", obj) at line 93. No HTML encoding, escaping, or output sanitization is applied to param/bar before it reaches the Writer sink. The switch on a hardcoded 'ABC' string is dead-code obfuscation but statically resolves to include the tainted branch, so the flow is real and reachable.",
