        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string parameter is decoded and written directly to the HTTP response via getWriter().format() without any HTML/context-appropriate output encoding, allowing injection of arbitrary script content into the response body.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious payload in the 'BenchmarkTest00800' query parameter that gets reflected unescaped in the response, enabling reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks such as session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary JavaScript execution in the victim's browser context.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode the 'bar' value before writing it to the response (e.g., using OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Avoid writing directly to the raw OutputStream/Writer with untrusted data; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Validate/allowlist the expected format of the parameter value before use.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers to reduce impact of any residual XSS."
        ]
      }
