        "exploitability_evidence": "The sink is Runtime.exec(cmd + bar, ...) at line 87-88. bar is assigned from either a hardcoded constant \"This_should_always_happen\" or from param (URL-decoded value derived from request.getQueryString(), attacker-controlled). However, the assignment is guarded by 'if ((7 * 42) - num > 200) bar = \"This_should_always_happen\"; else bar = param;'. Since num=86, (7*42)-num = 294-86 = 208, and 208 > 200 is always true, so bar is unconditionally assigned the constant string \"This_should_always_happen\" \u2014 the else branch containing tainted param is dead code and never executes. Therefore the tainted param value never reaches the exec() sink; only the constant string does.",
