      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "The flagged sink is Runtime.exec(args) where args includes 'bar', which originates from param = scr.getTheValue(\"BenchmarkTest00905\"). The called method body for SeparateClassRequest.getTheValue is shown and it unconditionally returns the hardcoded string literal \"bar\" regardless of any HTTP request parameter \u2014 it does NOT extract a value from the HttpServletRequest at all. Thus the value flowing into cmd/args at the exec() call is a compile-time constant, not attacker-controlled input, despite the SAST tool's generic pattern match on HttpServletRequest-derived helper classes. There is no actual taint reaching the sink in this specific test case.",
