        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled cookie value flows through URL-decoding into a File path construction without any path traversal-specific validation (e.g., canonicalization + prefix check or filename-only extraction) before being used to build a File object.",
        "impact": "An attacker can supply a cookie value containing directory traversal sequences (e.g., '../') to probe or reference files outside the intended TESTFILES_DIR, potentially confirming existence of arbitrary files on the filesystem, and combined with other unsafe operations elsewhere in the app, could lead to path traversal-based information disclosure.",
        "remediation": [
          "Canonicalize the resulting File path (getCanonicalPath()) and verify it still resides within the intended base directory (Utils.TESTFILES_DIR) before use.",
          "Use org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(bar) to strip any directory components from user input before constructing the File object.",
          "Maintain an allow-list of valid file names/identifiers instead of accepting arbitrary path segments from user input.",
          "Reject or reject-and-log any input containing '..' or path separators before it reaches file path construction."
        ]
      }
    },
