        "impact": "An attacker can supply a cookie value containing directory traversal sequences (e.g. '../../etc/passwd') to read arbitrary files on the filesystem that the application process has access to, leading to information disclosure of sensitive files.",
        "remediation": [
          "Sanitize/validate the decoded cookie value before using it in a file path \u2014 reject or strip path traversal sequences such as '../' and null bytes.",
          "Use java.nio.file.Path.normalize() combined with a check that the resolved path stays within the intended base directory (Utils.TESTFILES_DIR).",
          "Alternatively use org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(...) to strip any directory components and only use the bare file name.",
          "Avoid deriving file paths directly from user input; use an indirect reference (e.g., an ID mapped server-side to a fixed set of allowed files)."
        ]
      }
    },
