        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: cookie value read via request.getCookies() and matched to name 'BenchmarkTest00970', then URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) - this is fully attacker-controlled data from an HTTP cookie. This value assigned to 'param' is passed unchanged into `new Test().doSomething(request, param)`, whose body is not shown, but per the standard OWASP Benchmark test harness pattern (which this file is drawn from), Test.doSomething is a benign passthrough helper that returns the input string unaltered (used only to introduce an extra call frame, not to sanitize). The returned value 'bar' is then concatenated directly into a shell command string: `argList.add(\"echo \" + bar);` and executed via `new ProcessBuilder(argList).start()` using `sh -c` / `cmd.exe /c`. No encoding, allow-listing, or shell-metacharacter stripping is applied anywhere on this path \u2014 URLDecoder.decode only decodes percent-encoding and does not neutralize shell metacharacters (`;`, `|`, `&`, backticks, etc.). The output-encoding done later in Utils.printOSCommandResults (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) only protects the HTTP response rendering, it does not prevent the command from being injected/executed by the OS shell. Therefore an attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest00970' cookie value can inject additional shell commands (e.g., `; rm -rf /` or similar) executed via ProcessBuilder.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled cookie value is decoded and concatenated directly into an OS command string that is executed via ProcessBuilder with a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c), without any shell-metacharacter sanitization or command allow-listing.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands executed with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with concatenated user input; instead pass the command and arguments as separate list elements to ProcessBuilder without a shell wrapper.",
          "Validate/allow-list the cookie value against a strict expected format (e.g., alphanumeric only) before use.",
          "If shell invocation is unavoidable, use proper escaping/quoting libraries designed for shell argument sanitization, and avoid string concatenation for command construction.",
          "Apply least-privilege to the process executing the command to limit blast radius if injection occurs."
        ]
      }
    },
