      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP cookie named 'BenchmarkTest00978' read via request.getCookies(), URL-decoded into 'param'. This tainted value is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) and returned as 'bar' (Benchmark's Test.doSomething is a pass-through wrapper that returns the input unchanged, as is standard in these OWASP Benchmark test cases). 'bar' is then concatenated directly into the exec argument array: for non-Windows, args = {\"sh\",\"-c\", cmd + bar} where cmd is just 'ping -c1 ' (or 'cmd.exe /c ping -c1 ' on Windows) via Utils.getOSCommandString, which performs no sanitization \u2014 it only prepends a static command string. The resulting args array is passed unmodified to Runtime.getRuntime().exec(args). No validation, allow-listing, or escaping is applied to 'bar' anywhere on this path before it reaches the exec sink, so a cookie value like '; rm -rf /' or '&& malicious' would be interpreted by the shell (via 'sh -c') and injected into the command.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled cookie value is decoded and concatenated directly into a shell command string that is executed via Runtime.exec with 'sh -c'/'cmd.exe /c', without any sanitization, escaping, or allow-listing of the value before it reaches the OS command execution sink.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands by crafting the 'BenchmarkTest00978' cookie value, leading to arbitrary command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process, potentially resulting in full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell with user-controlled input; use ProcessBuilder with a fixed command and pass arguments as separate array elements without shell interpretation (avoid 'sh -c'/'cmd.exe /c').",
          "Validate and allow-list the cookie value against a strict set of expected values before using it in any command.",
          "If dynamic input must be used, strip or reject shell metacharacters (;, &, |, `, $, etc.) using a robust encoder/validator designed for OS command contexts.",
          "Consider using Java APIs (e.g., InetAddress.isReachable for ping-like functionality) instead of shelling out to OS commands."
        ]
      }
    },
