        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP cookie 'BenchmarkTest00980' value is read from request.getCookies(), URL-decoded, and stored in 'param'. This tainted string is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose result 'bar' is placed into argsEnv = {bar}. Runtime.getRuntime().exec(args, argsEnv) is then invoked with args={cmd} (a fixed script path from getInsecureOSCommandString, not attacker-controlled) and argsEnv containing the tainted 'bar' value as the environment for the spawned process. No sanitizer, whitelist check, or encoding is applied to 'bar' before it reaches Runtime.exec; ESAPI encodeForHTML is only used later on the *output* of the process for the HTTP response, which does not neutralize command/environment injection on the way in. The body of Test.doSomething is not shown, but in this benchmark's convention this helper is a pass-through wrapper and does not perform command-injection-specific validation. Because tainted cookie data flows unmodified into the exec() call (as an environment variable to a spawned process, still attacker-influenced content passed to Runtime.exec), this matches the CWE-78 sink pattern the rule targets.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied cookie value is decoded and forwarded (via a pass-through helper) into Runtime.exec's environment-variable array without any validation, whitelisting, or sanitization suitable for OS command/environment injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest00980' cookie value can inject arbitrary content into the environment of the spawned process; depending on how the invoked script (insecureCmd.sh/.bat) consumes that environment variable, this can lead to command injection, information disclosure, or arbitrary command execution on the server.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid passing user-controlled data into Runtime.exec/ProcessBuilder command arrays or environment variables entirely.",
          "If unavoidable, validate the input against a strict allow-list of expected values/characters before use.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed, parameterized command and pass user data only as a properly escaped single argument, never as raw environment content.",
          "Ensure any downstream script does not blindly evaluate or execute environment variable content."
        ]
      }
