      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: cookie value read via request.getCookies() for cookie name 'BenchmarkTest00983', URL-decoded and stored in 'param'. This tainted value flows through 'bar = new Test().doSomething(request, param)' (body not shown, but Benchmark's Test.doSomething() helpers are typically identity pass-throughs with no real sanitization) and is placed into the array 'argsEnv = {bar}'. This array is passed to 'Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd, argsEnv)'. While 'cmd' itself is a fixed, non-tainted path to insecureCmd.bat/sh (from Utils.getInsecureOSCommandString), the exec(String, String[]) overload treats the second argument as the environment variable array (envp) for the spawned process, not as command-line arguments. No validation, whitelist, or encoding is applied to 'bar' before it reaches this sink. An attacker who fully controls the cookie value can supply a string in the form 'NAME=VALUE' (e.g., 'PATH=/tmp/evil') to poison the child process's environment, potentially redirecting the invoked script's unqualified command calls to attacker-controlled binaries or otherwise manipulating process behavior \u2014 a recognized OS command/environment injection vector. No sanitizer of any kind (URLDecoder is not a security control) is applied on this path before the exec call.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Cookie-derived, URL-decoded, unsanitized user input is passed as the environment array (envp) to Runtime.exec(), with no validation, whitelist, or format checking of the value before it reaches the process-creation sink.",
        "impact": "An attacker controlling the cookie value could inject or override environment variables of the spawned process (e.g., PATH, LD_PRELOAD-like vectors depending on OS/script), potentially causing the invoked script to execute attacker-controlled binaries or otherwise manipulate process behavior, leading to command/code execution or information disclosure.",
        "remediation": [
          "Do not pass user-controlled data directly as process environment variables or command arguments.",
          "If dynamic environment configuration is required, use a strict whitelist of allowed variable names/values.",
          "Validate that any user-supplied value matches an expected safe pattern before use.",
          "Avoid exec() overloads that accept raw environment arrays built from untrusted input; prefer ProcessBuilder with an explicit, fixed environment and sanitized arguments.",
          "Apply centralized input validation/encoding appropriate for OS command contexts (e.g., ESAPI Validator) prior to use in any exec-related API."
        ]
      }
    },
