          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest01023.java:64:21-64:58:java.lang.security.audit.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "Attacker-controlled HTTP header is URL-decoded and passed through an intermediate method into an LDAP filter string without sanitization, enabling LDAP injection despite the presence of a parameterized placeholder for a different filter com",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.908
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01023\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header). It is URL-decoded then passed as 'param' into 'new Test().doSomething(request, param)', whose return value 'bar' flows directly into the LDAP filter string: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=\" + bar + \")(street={0}))\". This filter is passed to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc) \u2014 the flagged LDAP sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping of *, (, ), \\, NUL per RFC 4515) is applied to 'bar' before it is concatenated into the filter. The only encoding seen later in the method is org.owasp.esapi.ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(), which is applied to output values displayed in the HTTP response, not to the filter string used in the LDAP query itself. The Test.doSomething helper body is not shown, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this class is a pass-through wrapper that does not sanitize; even if it applied trivial transformations, there is no evidence of LDAP-specific sanitization on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled header value is decoded and concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping/sanitization before being used in DirContext.search().",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', ')', '(', '|') to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query constraints, extracting unauthorized directory data, or manipulating LDAP tree queries (LDAP injection).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a proper LDAP encoding routine (e.g., ESAPI's encoder().encodeForLDAP()) on the untrusted 'bar' value before inserting it into the filter string.",
          "Prefer parameterized/templated LDAP search filters (using the {0}, {1} placeholder mechanism already used for 'street') for all user-supplied values instead of string concatenation.",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected format of the header value (e.g., restrict to alphanumeric characters) before using it in any LDAP query."
        ]
      }
    },
