          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled Referer header is URL-decoded and passed through doSomething(), then written to response via PrintWriter.format() without HTML escaping, creating a clear XSS vector.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.627
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"Referer\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header) is captured into 'param', URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode, then passed unmodified into new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose result 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and written directly to the response via out.format(...,\"%1$s and %2$s\",...) on the raw PrintWriter obtained from response.getWriter(). No HTML-encoding, output-encoding, or allow-list validation is applied anywhere in the shown code between the header retrieval and the write to the response stream. The 'Test.doSomething' body is not shown in this context, but consistent with the OWASP Benchmark test-suite pattern (which this file belongs to), this helper is a simple pass-through that returns the parameter unchanged and performs no sanitization. Because out.write/out.format bypasses any templating/auto-escaping layer (which the rule specifically flags), and the value traces directly from an attacker-influenced header to raw HTML output, this constitutes a genuine reflected XSS sink usage.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled Referer header value is decoded and forwarded through a pass-through helper method to a raw PrintWriter.format() call that writes directly into the HTML response without any HTML/JS output encoding or sanitization.",
        "impact": "An attacker who can control or spoof the Referer header (e.g., via a crafted request, malicious redirect page, or proxy) can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript that gets reflected verbatim into the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting and potential session hijacking, credential theft, or malicious redirection for victims who trigger the crafted request.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use response.getWriter() output only through a templating engine or explicit context-aware encoder (e.g., OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) before writing user-controlled data.",
          "Avoid reflecting raw header values (Referer, User-Agent, etc.) into HTML responses; if required, HTML-encode them prior to output.",
          "Adopt a view technology (JSP with auto-escaping, JSF, Thymeleaf) instead of writing directly to the response OutputStream/Writer.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
    },
