          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled input from request header is URL-decoded and passed through an untrusted function, then written directly to response without HTML escaping, creating a plausible XSS vector.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.496
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"Referer\") is attacker-controlled and assigned to param. It is then URL-decoded via java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") (decoding does not sanitize/escape). It is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param); the body of Test.doSomething is not shown, but per OWASP Benchmark test conventions this helper is a pass-through/no-op that returns the tainted value largely unchanged. The result 'bar' is concatenated directly into a string and written via response.getWriter().write(\"Parameter value: \" + bar) at line 54 with no HTML encoding, no output escaping, and no allow-list validation applied anywhere on the path. This is a direct write to the raw response Writer bypassing any templating/escaping layer, matching the sink pattern for CWE-79.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP header value (Referer) is decoded and concatenated into an HTTP response body via response.getWriter().write() without any HTML/context-aware output encoding or sanitization.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a Referer header containing HTML/JavaScript payloads that will be reflected verbatim in the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) executed in the victim's browser context, potentially leading to session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode all user-controlled data before writing to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Avoid writing directly to the raw response Writer/OutputStream; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Validate/allow-list the Referer header format if it must be reflected, and reject or strip unexpected characters.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers to reduce impact of any residual XSS."
        ]
      }
    },
