        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Attacker-controlled HTTP header data flows unsanitized into the envp parameter of Runtime.exec, allowing arbitrary environment variable injection into a spawned OS process.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the environment of the spawned process (e.g., PATH, IFS, LD_PRELOAD) potentially causing execution of attacker-supplied binaries or altering command resolution/behavior, leading to remote code execution or other OS-level compromise.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid passing user-controlled data as process environment variables; if required, strictly whitelist allowed variable names/values.",
          "Use a fixed, minimal, and trusted environment array (envp) instead of incorporating request data.",
          "Validate/canonicalize any user input against an allow-list before use in any exec-related parameter.",
          "Avoid invoking external OS commands/scripts altogether when possible; prefer safe Java APIs."
        ]
