        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01083\") is read into 'param' (attacker-controlled HTTP header), then URL-decoded. The decoded value is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) which returns 'bar' - this Test helper class in the OWASP Benchmark suite is a pass-through utility that does not perform any SQL-specific sanitization (its body wasn't shown but no encodeForSQL/whitelist call is applied before or after in the focal method). 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME=? and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". Although a PreparedStatement object is created via connection.prepareStatement(sql, ...), the only bound parameter is statement.setString(1, \"foo\") for the '?' placeholder - the attacker-controlled 'bar' value is embedded directly into the SQL text itself via string concatenation, not passed as a bound parameter. statement.execute() then executes this attacker-influenced SQL string. No sanitizer, allow-list, or escaping function is applied to 'bar' or 'param' anywhere on this path before it reaches the SQL sink.",
