      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01098\") -> URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode -> passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) which in the standard OWASP Benchmark suite is a pass-through helper that returns the tainted value unmodified (its class name and pattern indicate no sanitization is applied) -> assigned to 'bar' -> directly concatenated into the SQL string 'INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')' -> executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql, ...) using a plain java.sql.Statement (not PreparedStatement). No escaping, allow-listing, or parameterization occurs anywhere on this path before the SQL execution sink. The only sanitizer present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later, only for HTML output of the completed query, not before the SQL execution \u2014 so it does not mitigate the injection.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP header value is URL-decoded and concatenated directly into a SQL INSERT statement string, which is then executed with a raw Statement instead of a parameterized PreparedStatement, allowing SQL syntax injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the header value to manipulate the INSERT statement, potentially inserting malicious data, breaking out of the intended query to execute additional SQL commands (depending on driver/batch support), or corrupting the users table.",
        "remediation": [
          "Replace java.sql.Statement with a PreparedStatement and bind 'bar' as a parameter (e.g., INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo', ?)).",
          "Do not concatenate untrusted input directly into SQL strings.",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected format of the header value before use.",
          "Ensure any pass-through helper methods (like Test.doSomething) do not silently forward untrusted data without validation."
        ]
      }
    },
