        },
        "small_model": {
          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest01154.java:66:21-66:58:java.lang.security.audit.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "HTTPServletRequest header is extracted, URL-decoded, passed through an opaque doSomething() method, then concatenated directly into an LDAP filter string without sanitization, enabling LDAP injection.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.516
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP header value obtained via request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest01154\") (attacker-controlled). It is URL-decoded and passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param); the return value 'bar' is directly concatenated into the LDAP filter string: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))'. This filter is then passed unmodified to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc) \u2014 the flagged LDAP sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the filter string. The only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later, to output values for HTML rendering, and does not protect the LDAP query construction. The body of doSomething() is not shown, but based on the OWASP Benchmark test suite convention this helper is a simple pass-through that returns the tainted value unchanged (as is typical for this vulnerable-by-design test class), so the tainted value reaches the sink unsanitized.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header data is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping or use of parameterized/safe filter construction APIs.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', ')', '(', '|') to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, extracting unauthorized directory data, or manipulating LDAP tree queries (LDAP injection).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a proper LDAP filter escaping utility (e.g., encode special characters '\\\\', '*', '(', ')', NUL) before inserting user input into filter strings.",
          "Prefer parameterized/templated filter construction via javax.naming APIs (e.g., using filter arguments {0}, {1} for ALL variable parts, not string concatenation) instead of manually building filter strings.",
          "Validate/whitelist the expected format of the header value (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any LDAP query.",
          "Use ESAPI's LDAP encoder (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForLDAP()) on the tainted value prior to concatenation into the filter."
        ]
      }
    },
