        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: the 'Referer' request header (attacker-controlled, e.g. via crafted HTTP request) is read via request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") into 'param'. It is then URL-decoded (URLDecoder.decode does not perform any HTML/XSS sanitization) and passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param), whose body is not shown/available in the provided context, so no sanitization can be confirmed there. The returned value 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and written directly to the response via response.getWriter().printf(...) with no HTML encoding applied anywhere on the path. Because printf just performs string formatting (no escaping) and the value ends up in the HTTP response body, this is a direct source-to-sink flow of unsanitized data into the page.",
