        "impact": "An attacker can craft a request with a malicious Referer header (or induce a victim's browser to send one, e.g. via a crafted link/page) containing HTML/JavaScript payloads; when reflected unescaped in the response, this results in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), allowing script execution in the victim's browser context, session hijacking, credential theft, or defacement.",
