        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Untrusted dataP header data flows through URURL dececocoding and a pass-through helper method into the environment-variable argument of Runntime.exec without without any sanitization, validation, or whitelisting, allowing injection of arbitrary environment variable name/value content into the spawned OS process.",
        "impact": "An attacker who controls the HTTP header value could inject arbitrary environment variable entries into the executed subprocess (e.g., manipulating PATH, hooks, or other variables the script relies on), potentially altering process behavior, leaking data, or achieving code execution depending on how the invoked script/environment is used, consistent with OS command injection risk.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid passing user-controlled data into Runtime.exec's environment array or command array entirely.",
          "If environment customization is required, whitelist allowed variable names/values and reject anything not matching the whitelist.",
          "Validate and strictly sanitize the header value (e.g., allow only a fixed set of alphanumeric characters) before any use in process execution context.",
          "Use higher-level APIs (ProcessBuilder with a fixed, vetted command and no dynamic environment injection from user input) instead of constructing envp from request data."
        ]
      }
