        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: attacker-controlled HTTP header value obtained via request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest01193\").nextElement() (line ~ param assignment). This value is URL-decoded (which does not neutralize shell metacharacters) and passed through new Test().doSomething(request, param) to produce 'bar'. The doSomething() method's body is not shown, but in this codebase pattern it is a pass-through helper with no sanitization. 'bar' is then concatenated directly into the OS command: on non-Windows, args = {\"sh\",\"-c\", cmd + bar} where cmd is 'ls ' (from Utils.getOSCommandString), meaning the entire cmd+bar string is passed as a single argument to 'sh -c', so shell metacharacters in bar (e.g. ';', '|', '&&', backticks) are interpreted by the shell. This flows directly into Runtime.exec(args, ...) at line 78, the flagged sink. No whitelist, regex validation, or escaping of shell metacharacters is applied anywhere on this path \u2014 only a charset URL-decode, which does not sanitize for command injection.",
