        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header value is decoded and concatenated into a command string that is executed via 'sh -c', without neutralizing shell metacharacters, enabling OS command injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can execute arbitrary OS commands on the server by injecting shell metacharacters into the custom HTTP header, potentially leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with user-controlled input; use exec() with an argument array and no shell interpretation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the header value against a strict allow-list of expected characters or values before use.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed command and pass user input only as a discrete, non-shell-interpreted argument.",
