        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP header 'BenchmarkTest01216' obtained via request.getHeaders(...), URL-decoded, then passed through new Test().doSomething(request, param) (pass-through helper, no sanitization shown) into 'bar'. 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" and executed via statement.addBatch(sql) / statement.executeBatch() using a plain java.sql.Statement rather than a PreparedStatement. No escaping, parameterization, or input validation occurs on this path before the SQL execution, so an attacker-supplied header value containing a single quote can break out of the string literal and inject arbitrary SQL.",
