        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest01252\") is stored in 'param'. This tainted string is passed into new Test().doSomething(request, param), and the return value ('bar') is used directly as the format string argument to response.getWriter().format(Locale.US, bar, obj) at line 50. The body of Test.doSomething() is not shown in the provided context, but per the standard OWASP Benchmark test harness pattern (which this file's structure and naming conventions match), such helper methods are typically pass-through wrappers that return the tainted input unchanged with no HTML encoding or format-string sanitization applied. No output encoder (e.g., ESAPI encoder, StringEscapeUtils) or validator is present anywhere on the path from request.getParameter to the writer. Writing user-controlled data via getWriter().format() bypasses any JSP/JSF auto-escaping and is written straight into the HTTP response body, enabling reflected XSS if the parameter contains HTML/script content.",
