        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands or command arguments that execute with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full server compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid building shell command strings from user input; use ProcessBuilder with an explicit, fixed argument array instead of concatenating strings.",
          "Validate the parameter against a strict allow-list of expected values before use.",
          "If command execution with variable input is unavoidable, use OS-level APIs that do not invoke a shell interpreter, and escape/reject any shell metacharacters.",
          "Ensure Test.doSomething() (and any other helper touching tainted input) performs input validation/sanitization before returning the value for use in security-sensitive sinks."
        ]
      }
