        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into a SQL statement string used to build a CallableStatement, without parameterization or input validation.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL/stored-procedure call syntax via the 'BenchmarkTest01301' parameter, potentially leading to unauthorized data access, data modification, or database compromise.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries/PreparedStatement or CallableStatement placeholders (?) instead of string concatenation for any user-supplied value.",
          "Validate/allowlist the input if it must select a stored procedure or table name, since bind parameters cannot parameterize identifiers.",
          "Apply strict input validation (e.g., regex allowlist) on the parameter before using it in any SQL context.",
          "Enable least-privilege DB accounts and prepared statement caching to reduce injection impact."
        ]
