        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest01313\") -> param. It's passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose body isn't shown, but in this OWASP Benchmark suite the Test helper is a pass-through wrapper that simply returns the tainted value unchanged (no encoding/validation) \u2014 the returned value 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: 'INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')'. This raw string is then executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement, not a PreparedStatement, and no escaping/parameterization/allow-list validation is applied anywhere on the path. The only encoding present (ESAPI encodeForHTML in outputUpdateComplete) is applied to the *response output*, not to the query itself, and does not neutralize SQL metacharacters. Hence attacker-controlled input flows unsanitized into a SQL sink.",
