      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP request parameter map.get(\"BenchmarkTest01326\") is read into 'param'. This value is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose implementation is not shown (only LDAPManager methods are provided as 'Called project methods'), so it must be treated as an untrusted pass-through per typical Benchmark helper patterns. The result 'bar' is directly string-concatenated into an LDAP filter: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))' with no LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., no encodeForLDAP, no character whitelist/regex validation) applied to 'bar' before it is used. This filter string is then passed straight to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc), which is exactly the DirContext.search sink flagged for LDAP injection. The only encoding present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later to attribute values displayed in the HTTP response, which protects against XSS, not LDAP injection, so it does not neutralize the tainted data before it reaches the LDAP search sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled request parameter is concatenated unescaped into an LDAP search filter string that is passed to DirContext.search, with no LDAP-specific sanitization or escaping applied to neutralize special filter characters (e.g., '(', ')', '*', '\\\\').",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters to alter query logic (e.g., bypass filters, extract additional directory attributes, or manipulate boolean logic of the search), potentially exposing or manipulating LDAP directory data.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use ESAPI's encodeForLDAP (or equivalent LDAP-safe encoder) on the tainted parameter before including it in the filter string.",
          "Prefer parameterized/paramaterized LDAP filter APIs (using filterArgs / {0} placeholders) for all attacker-controlled values instead of string concatenation.",
          "Validate/whitelist input against an expected character set (e.g., alphanumeric) before using it in directory queries.",
          "Verify what Test.doSomething() actually does with the input; if it does not sanitize, apply sanitization at the point where 'bar' is used to build the filter."
        ]
      }
    },
