      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() value for key 'BenchmarkTest01353' assigned to 'param' (attacker-controlled HTTP parameter). This raw param is passed to 'new Test().doSomething(request, param)' whose body is not shown, but no sanitizer/validator method is invoked on the path afterward. The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into a shell command string: argList.add(\"echo \" + bar), which is then executed via new ProcessBuilder().command(argList).start(). The command is invoked through a shell interpreter ('sh -c' or 'cmd.exe /c'), meaning any shell metacharacters (;, |, `, $()) in the parameter value will be interpreted by the shell. No encoding/escaping for shell metacharacters is applied anywhere in the shown code prior to the ProcessBuilder call; the only encoding present (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied later to the *output* of the command for the HTTP response, not to the command input itself, so it does not mitigate the injection.",
