      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "User-controlled data flows from request.getParameterMap() -> param -> Test().doSomething(request, param) -> bar. However, bar is placed into argsEnv = {bar}, which is passed as the SECOND argument to Runtime.exec(String[] cmdarray, String[] envp). In the Java API, the second array parameter of Runtime.exec(cmdarray, envp) is the environment-variable array (envp), not additional command-line arguments to be executed. The actual command array (args = {cmd}) is built entirely from Utils.getInsecureOSCommandString(), which resolves a fixed file path (insecureCmd.bat/insecureCmd.sh) from the classpath \u2014 this value is not attacker-controlled. Since bar only supplies environment-variable data to the spawned process rather than being concatenated into or substituted as part of the executed command line, it is not interpreted by a shell as command syntax. No evidence in the shown code (including Utils.printOSCommandResults, which only reads/prints command output) indicates the target script itself evaluates or executes the environment variable content. Therefore the tainted value does not reach a genuine command-injection sink.",
        "verdict": "False Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The tainted user input is passed as the envp parameter (environment variables) of Runtime.exec(String[] cmdarray, String[] envp), not as part of the cmdarray that is actually executed/interpreted by the OS shell. Environment variable values are not parsed as shell commands, so no command injection occurs via this parameter regardless of sanitization applied to it.",
        "impact": "None via this specific sink \u2014 the value cannot alter or inject into the OS command being executed since it is only exposed to the child process as an environment variable, not as command syntax.",
        "remediation": [
          "Verify that the target script (insecureCmd.sh/insecureCmd.bat) does not itself read and execute/evaluate the passed environment variable value.",
          "If user input must be passed to child processes, avoid using it in either cmdarray or envp without strict allow-listing/validation.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with explicit, fixed commands and validated arguments rather than free-form environment injection.",
          "Confirm the behavior of Test.doSomething() to ensure no additional unsafe use of the parameter occurs elsewhere."
        ]
      }
