      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() at line 43 extracts the 'BenchmarkTest01375' parameter into 'param' (fully attacker-controlled). This value is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) (line 49), whose return value 'bar' is stored directly into the HTTP session via request.getSession().putValue('userid', bar) at line 53 \u2014 the flagged sink. The body of Test.doSomething() is not shown, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper class is a pass-through/obfuscation wrapper that returns the tainted parameter largely unchanged; there is no validation or sanitization of 'bar' before it is placed into the session object. The only sanitization visible in the file \u2014 Utils.encodeForHTML(bar) \u2014 is applied afterward, purely for HTML output encoding in the response, and does not run before or in place of the putValue() call. Thus, unvalidated user input reaches the session-storage sink unsanitized, satisfying the CWE-501 Trust Boundary Violation pattern.",
