        "remediation": [
          "Use a parameterized query for all user-controlled values: replace the string concatenation of `bar` with a second `?` placeholder and bind it via `statement.setString(2, bar)` instead of concatenating into the SQL text.",
          "Never build SQL command text by concatenating unsanitized request parameters; treat all data from HttpServletRequest as untrusted.",
          "If dynamic SQL is unavoidable, apply strict input validation (e.g., allow-list) or use an established SQL-escaping library, but prefer parameter binding wherever possible.",
          "Add automated tests / static-analysis gating to catch string-concatenated SQL statements before they reach production."
