      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: the servlet reads all HTTP request parameter names/values via request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() and picks the parameter name whose value equals a fixed marker string; that parameter name 'param' is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param), which (following the standard OWASP Benchmark helper pattern) retrieves and returns the raw value of request.getParameter(param) as 'bar'. 'bar' is then concatenated directly into the LDAP search filter string: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))' with no LDAP-specific escaping (e.g. no escaping of '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) before being passed to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc). The only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later to output written back to the HTTP response, not to 'bar' before it is embedded in the LDAP filter, so it provides no protection against LDAP injection. The parameterized substitution array ('filters') only covers the {0} placeholder for 'street', not the concatenated 'uid=' + bar segment, so attacker-controlled input directly alters the filter syntax (e.g., closing/opening parentheses to inject additional filter clauses).",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP request parameter value is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping or use of a safe parameterized filter mechanism for that portion of the query.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters to alter the search logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, retrieving unauthorized directory entries, or in some LDAP implementations causing further information disclosure.",
        "remediation": [
          "Escape LDAP special characters (e.g., '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) in user input before embedding it in a filter string, e.g., using ESAPI's encodeForLDAP() or an equivalent LDAP filter encoder.",
          "Use fully parameterized filter expressions (placeholders like {0}, {1}) for all user-controlled portions of the query instead of string concatenation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the expected format of the parameter value (e.g., restrict to alphanumeric characters) before use in the filter."
        ]
      }
    },
