      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP request parameters via request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() are enumerated to find the parameter name whose value equals a fixed marker string; that parameter NAME is then passed into `new Test().doSomething(request, param)`. In the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper simply returns `request.getParameter(param)` (attacker-controlled value) without any sanitization. The returned value `bar` is concatenated directly into an OS command string `\"echo \" + bar` and passed as an argument array element to `new ProcessBuilder(args)`, which is then executed via `pb.start()` at line 77 \u2014 the flagged sink. No validation, whitelist check, or escaping of shell metacharacters is performed on `bar` before it reaches ProcessBuilder. The only sanitization present (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied later to the *output* of the process for HTML display, which does nothing to prevent command injection at the exec sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter value is used unsanitized to build a shell command string executed via ProcessBuilder, allowing injection of arbitrary shell metacharacters/commands.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject shell metacharacters (e.g., `; rm -rf /` or `$(malicious command)`) into the parameter value, resulting in arbitrary OS command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking shell commands with user-controlled input; use safer Java APIs to accomplish the task (e.g., avoid shelling out to 'echo').",
          "If command execution is required, do not pass user input as part of a shell string; use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and pass user data only as a properly separated argument, and validate against a strict whitelist of allowed characters/values.",
          "Reject or strip shell metacharacters (;, |, &, $, `, >, <, etc.) from the input before use.",
          "Run the subprocess with the minimum required privileges and without invoking a shell interpreter (avoid 'sh -c' or 'cmd.exe /c')."
        ]
      }
    },
