        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() enumeration finds a parameter whose value equals 'BenchmarkTest01443' and captures its name into 'param'. This is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param), whose body is not shown, but per the OWASP Benchmark suite pattern this helper simply returns request.getParameter(param) (attacker-controlled) unmodified into 'bar'. 'bar' is then concatenated with an OS-command prefix (cmd) and passed directly to Runtime.exec(cmd + bar, argsEnv) at line 72 with no validation, whitelist check, or shell-metacharacter sanitization anywhere on the path. The only sanitizer visible in the file (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied only to command *output* for HTML display, not to the input string used to build the command, so it does not mitigate the injection.",
