        "impact": "An attacker who controls the HTTP request parameter can inject arbitrary OS command arguments or shell metacharacters (depending on how bar/doSomething handles it), leading to arbitrary command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid building OS commands from user input; use a whitelist of allowed values or an enum-based mapping instead of raw request data.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and pass user data only as a discrete argument (never concatenated into a single command string), and disable shell interpretation.",
          "Validate/normalize the parameter value against a strict allow-list before use.",
          "Run the process with least privilege and consider sandboxing to limit blast radius if injection still occurs."
