        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-influenced data (HTTP request parameter name/value obtained via Test.doSomething) is concatenated directly into a SQL query string that is executed with java.sql.Statement.addBatch/executeBatch instead of a parameterized PreparedStatement, with no sanitization or encoding applied before the SQL sink.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the HTTP request parameters to inject arbitrary SQL syntax into the WHERE clause of the query, potentially bypassing authentication, extracting or modifying data, or in some database configurations executing further malicious SQL.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a parameterized query (PreparedStatement) with bind variables instead of string concatenation for the SQL statement.",
          "Validate/allow-list the parameter name and value before use if dynamic behavior is required.",
          "Avoid using Statement.addBatch/executeBatch with untrusted, concatenated SQL text.",
          "Review the Test.doSomething() implementation to confirm it does not perform any sanitization, and add explicit input validation there if it returns raw request data."
        ]
      }
