        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The flagged sink at line 86 (response.getWriter().println(value.getTextContent() + \"<br/>\")) outputs text content parsed from a static classpath XML file (employees.xml), not the attacker-controlled `bar`/`param` value itself. The only place `bar` (derived from user input) is written to the response is in the catch block, where it is explicitly passed through ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(bar) before being printed, which is an adequate HTML encoder for this sink. The semgrep rule 'no-direct-response-writer' is a generic pattern match on any writer.println with a variable, and here it misfires because the variable content actually originates from server-controlled XML data, not reflected user input.",
