      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HttpServletRequest parameter 'BenchmarkTest01490' obtained via scr.getTheParameter() (SeparateClassRequest.getTheParameter simply returns request.getParameter(p)), assigned to 'param'. It is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) and the result stored in 'bar' (Test.doSomething body not shown, but no sanitizer is applied on 'bar' anywhere in the visible code \u2014 the OWASP Benchmark test pattern typically returns the tainted value unchanged). 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the LDAP search filter string: 'String filter = \"(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=\" + bar + \")(street={0}))\";' and passed to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc) at line 61 (the flagged sink). No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) is performed on 'bar' before it reaches the filter string \u2014 the only encoding present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied afterward to output values for HTML display, which is irrelevant to sanitizing LDAP filter syntax. Thus attacker-controlled input reaches the LDAP query construction unsanitized.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP metacharacter escaping/sanitization before being used in DirContext.search, allowing filter syntax to be altered by attacker input.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', '(', ')', '|', '&') to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, extracting unauthorized directory entries, or manipulating the LDAP query to return unintended results (LDAP injection).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized LDAP filters exclusively (as already partially done for the 'street' attribute via filters array/{0} placeholder) instead of string concatenation for the 'uid' value.",
          "Apply proper LDAP filter escaping (e.g., via javax.naming or a library like OWASP ESAPI's encodeForLDAP / Apache Commons Text's escapeLdapSearchFilter) to the 'bar' value before inserting it into the filter string.",
          "Validate/whitelist the expected format of the input parameter (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any directory query.",
          "Review the Test.doSomething() method to ensure it does not merely pass through tainted input without sanitization."
        ]
      }
    },
