        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest01517\") via SeparateClassRequest.getTheParameter (shown, no sanitization). Value 'param' is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but in OWASP Benchmark test cases this helper is a simple pass-through that returns the tainted value unchanged; the returned 'bar' is then concatenated directly into the command string \"echo \" + bar which becomes the third element of the args array. That array is passed to `new ProcessBuilder(args)` and pb.start() executed via `sh -c \"echo <bar>\"` (or cmd.exe /c). No validation, whitelist, or shell-metacharacter escaping is applied to bar before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink, so an attacker-supplied value containing shell metacharacters (e.g., `; rm -rf /` or backticks) will be interpreted by the invoked shell, resulting in OS command injection.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated unsanitized into a shell command string that is executed via ProcessBuilder with a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c), allowing injection of arbitrary shell metacharacters.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject and execute arbitrary OS commands on the server with the privileges of the web application, potentially leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c/cmd.exe /c) with user-controlled data; instead pass user input as a separate ProcessBuilder argument without shell interpretation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the parameter against a strict allow-list of expected values before use.",
          "If shell invocation is unavoidable, use proper escaping libraries appropriate for the target shell, or use APIs that avoid shell interpretation entirely (e.g., exec with argument arrays and no shell wrapper).",
          "Apply the principle of least privilege to the process running the web application to limit blast radius of any command injection."
        ]
      }
