      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HttpServletRequest parameter 'BenchmarkTest01517' obtained via scr.getTheParameter(...) which just returns request.getParameter(p) unmodified. This value 'param' is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) and returned as 'bar' (Test.doSomething's body is not shown, but per Benchmark's standard pattern these wrapper methods are pass-throughs that do not sanitize the value). 'bar' is then concatenated directly into a shell command string: args = {a1, a2, \"echo \" + bar}, where a1/a2 are 'sh'/'-c' (or 'cmd.exe'/'/c' on Windows). This array is passed straight into new ProcessBuilder(args).start(), meaning the untrusted 'bar' value is interpreted by a shell (sh -c ...) allowing metacharacters such as ; | & ` $() to break out of the intended 'echo' command. No validation, allow-listing, or escaping is applied to 'bar' anywhere on this path before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink, and Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the *output* of the command afterward, which does nothing to prevent the injection at execution time.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP request parameter flows unsanitized into a shell command executed via ProcessBuilder with 'sh -c' / 'cmd.exe /c', allowing shell metacharacters in the parameter to inject arbitrary additional commands.",
        "impact": "An attacker can supply a parameter value containing shell metacharacters (e.g., '; rm -rf /' or '$(malicious command)') to execute arbitrary OS commands with the privileges of the web application process, leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell to run OS commands with user-controlled input; if command execution is required, use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and pass user data only as individual, non-shell-interpreted arguments (avoid 'sh -c').",
          "Validate and allow-list the expected format/content of the parameter (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any command context.",
          "If shell invocation cannot be avoided, use a well-vetted escaping/quoting library specific to the target shell, and reject inputs containing shell metacharacters.",
          "Apply the principle of least privilege to the process executing the command to limit the impact of a successful injection."
        ]
      }
    },
