        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the request parameter (e.g., breaking out of the quoted PASSWORD literal) to bypass authentication, exfiltrate data from the USERS table, or manipulate/damage the database depending on DBMS privileges.",
        "remediation": [
          "Replace java.sql.Statement with a java.sql.PreparedStatement and bind the parameter using setString() rather than string concatenation.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the parameter if it is expected to match a limited format.",
          "Ensure Test.doSomething() does not simply pass through untrusted input without validation; audit its implementation to confirm no sanitization is silently relied upon."
        ]
      }
    },
