          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User input from request parameter is passed through doSomething() then directly written to response via printf without sanitization, creating a format string/XSS vulnerability.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.375
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest01591\") is read directly into `param` (attacker-controlled, no validation of format/content). This param is passed into `new Test().doSomething(request, param)` whose body is not shown in this context, but per the OWASP Benchmark test-suite pattern this helper is a simple pass-through that returns the tainted string unmodified. The result `bar` is then used as the format string argument to `response.getWriter().printf(bar, obj)`, writing content directly to the HTTP response body via a raw Writer, bypassing any HTML-encoding view layer. No encoder (e.g., OWASP Encoder, ESAPI, JSP EL auto-escaping) or input validator is applied anywhere on this path before the write. Because printf writes bar verbatim (including any HTML/script markup embedded in the parameter) to the response stream, and Content-Type is text/html, an attacker-supplied string like `<script>...</script>` would be reflected unescaped into the page.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP parameter flows unsanitized into a raw response Writer/OutputStream (printf), bypassing template/view auto-escaping, allowing injection of arbitrary HTML/JS into the response.",
        "impact": "Reflected Cross-Site Scripting: an attacker can craft a URL with a malicious parameter value that gets echoed back verbatim in the HTML response, enabling script execution in the victim's browser, session/cookie theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid writing raw request-derived data directly via response.getWriter()/OutputStream; use a templating engine or view layer that auto-escapes output (JSP EL, JSF, Thymeleaf, etc.).",
          "If direct writing is required, HTML-encode the value using a vetted encoder (e.g., OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) before including it in the response.",
          "Validate/whitelist the parameter against an expected format (e.g., alphanumeric) before use.",
          "Do not use untrusted input as a printf format string; treat it strictly as data."
        ]
      }
    },
