      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest01600\") is attacker-controlled and assigned to param. This is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) which returns bar (Test.doSomething is a standard OWASP Benchmark passthrough helper that returns the input essentially unmodified \u2014 no sanitization is shown or called anywhere in the visible code path). bar is then concatenated into the command string \"echo \" + bar which is added to argList as a single argument to be interpreted by a shell (sh -c or cmd.exe /c). Because the value is executed via a shell interpreter (-c flag) rather than as a literal argv element to a fixed binary, shell metacharacters (;, |, `, $(), &&, etc.) in bar will be interpreted by the shell, enabling OS command injection. No whitelist, encoding, or escaping is applied to bar before it reaches ProcessBuilder.start().",
