        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into a shell command string (\"echo \" + bar) that is executed via a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) through ProcessBuilder, without any input validation, sanitization, or whitelisting.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands by supplying shell metacharacters in the BenchmarkTest01600 parameter, leading to arbitrary command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process, potentially resulting in full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with user-controlled input; instead, pass command and arguments directly to ProcessBuilder without shell interpretation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the input against a strict set of allowed characters or known-good values before use.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, properly escape/quote the input for the target shell or use APIs that avoid shell metacharacter interpretation entirely.",
          "Avoid executing OS commands based on user input altogether where possible; use safer language-level APIs to accomplish the same task."
