        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest01607\") assigns user-controlled value to 'param'. This is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) and returned as 'bar' (Test.doSomething body not shown/tracked, but no sanitizer is visible on this path and the OWASP Benchmark harness for this test id typically returns the tainted value unchanged). 'bar' is then used to build the exec args: on non-Windows systems, args = {\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd + bar} \u2014 here 'cmd + bar' is concatenated into a single string that is handed to '/bin/sh -c', meaning the shell will interpret any metacharacters (e.g. ; | && `) contained in 'bar'. On Windows, args = {\"cmd.exe\", \"/c\", cmd, bar} \u2014 cmd.exe /c re-joins its trailing arguments into one command line and interprets it, so injected metacharacters in 'bar' are similarly effective. Runtime.getRuntime().exec(args) then executes this attacker-influenced command. No validation, whitelist, or shell-metacharacter encoding is applied to 'bar' anywhere in the shown code before it reaches exec(); the only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied to the *output* of the command for HTML display, which does not neutralize the command before execution.",
