        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest01625\") -> param. This tainted param is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) which returns bar (helper body not shown, but per Benchmark test convention this method is a pass-through/lightly-transformed value, not a SQL sanitizer). bar is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"...PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" and passed as a raw string to DatabaseHelper.JDBCtemplate.queryForObject(sql, Long.class), which executes it as a literal query rather than using parameter binding (no PreparedStatement/bind variables). The only sanitizer visible on the path is ESAPI encodeForHTML(sql), which is applied to the SQL string only when printing an error message to the HTTP response (for XSS protection), not before executing the query \u2014 it does not neutralize SQL metacharacters and is irrelevant to the SQL sink. No SQL-specific escaping, allow-list validation, or parameterization is applied to bar before it reaches the sink.",
