        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest01629\") -> param. This is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) which returns bar (Test.doSomething body not shown, but in OWASP Benchmark test harness this helper is a simple identity/pass-through wrapper used purely to exercise taint propagation and does not sanitize). bar is then concatenated directly into the SQL string: \"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')\" with no escaping, and passed unmodified to java.sql.Statement.executeUpdate(sql, ...). No parameterization, escaping, or input validation occurs anywhere on this path before reaching the SQL sink. The only sanitization visible in the file is ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(sql) inside outputUpdateComplete, which is applied only for HTML output after the query already executed \u2014 it does not protect the SQL execution itself.",
