          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User-controlled query parameter is decoded and passed through `Test.doSomething()` then written to response via `out.format()` without HTML escaping, creating a direct XSS vector.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.45
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> paramLoc lookup -> substring extraction -> URLDecoder.decode() produces 'param', which is fully attacker-controlled (query string value). This value is passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown in this context, so we cannot confirm any encoding is applied there; assuming it returns the value largely unmodified (typical of these Benchmark helper classes), the result 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and written directly to the response via out.format(...,'%1$s and %2$s.', obj) using java.io.PrintWriter obtained from response.getWriter(). No HTML-encoding, output escaping, or CWE-79-appropriate sanitizer is applied anywhere on this path before the value reaches the raw PrintWriter sink. This matches the classic Semgrep 'no-direct-response-writer' XSS pattern: user input flowing into an OutputStream/Writer bypassing template escaping.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query-string parameter is decoded and forwarded through an intermediate helper (Test.doSomething) whose implementation is not shown, then written directly to the response body via a raw PrintWriter/format call without any HTML encoding or output escaping, bypassing safe view/templating mechanisms.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious payload in the query string that gets reflected unescaped in the HTML response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary JavaScript execution in victims' browsers.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode/escape all user-controlled data before writing it to the response body (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() before formatting).",
          "Avoid writing directly to the raw PrintWriter/OutputStream for dynamic content; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF/Thymeleaf) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Set the 'X-XSS-Protection' header appropriately (do not disable it) and add a strict Content-Security-Policy as defense in depth.",
          "Verify and sanitize the return value of Test.doSomething() to ensure it never returns unescaped HTML-significant characters."
        ]
      }
    },
