        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string parameter is extracted, URL-decoded, and passed through an opaque helper method without any HTML output encoding before being written directly to the HTTP response writer, bypassing any templating/auto-escaping layer.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script payload as the BenchmarkTest01660 parameter; if reflected unescaped in the response body, this results in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), allowing session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary JavaScript execution in the victim's browser context.",
        "remediation": [
          "Apply context-appropriate output encoding (e.g., OWASP ESAPI Encoder.encodeForHTML()) to 'bar' before writing it to the response.",
          "Avoid writing raw user input directly via response.getWriter(); use a templating engine or view technology that auto-escapes output (e.g., JSP EL, JSF, Thymeleaf).",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected parameter format before use.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers to reduce XSS impact.",
          "Audit the Test.doSomething() helper method to ensure it does not simply pass through untrusted input unmodified."
        ]
      }
