      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> paramval extracted and URL-decoded via java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") -> passed to new Test().doSomething(request, param) -> result 'bar' returned and written directly to the response via response.getWriter().println(bar) at line 73. No HTML encoding, escaping, or output sanitization is applied to 'bar' before it is written to the HTTP response. The body of Test.doSomething() is not shown here, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper is typically a pass-through/transform that preserves the tainted value. Since no sanitizer is visible on the path shown and the sink is a raw response writer call, the flow is exploitable.",
