        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled query string parameter is URL-decoded and flows through an opaque helper method to be written directly into the HTTP response body without an OutputStream/Writer without without HTML escaping, bypassing any templating/auto-escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL query parameter containing HTML/JavaScript payload that, once decoded and echoed back unescaped in the response, executes in the victim's browser context, enabling reflected XSS (session hijacking, credential theft, defacement, etc.).",
