        "root_cause": "User-controlled query string parameter is decoded and concatenated directly into a shell command string executed via ProcessBuilder without any input validation, whitelisting, or escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands (e.g., via shell metacharacters like ; | & `` `) that get executed with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with concatenated user input; instead pass command and arguments as separate array elements without a shell wrapper.",
          "Validate/whitelist the parameter value against a strict allow-list of expected values before using it in any command.",
          "If shell invocation is unavoidable, properly escape/quote the user-supplied value or reject any input containing shell metacharacters.",
          "Use a well-vetted library or API that avoids OS command execution altogether for this functionality."
        ]
      }
    },
