        "impact": "An attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest01686' query parameter can inject arbitrary content into the environment passed to the executed OS script; if that script consumes the environment variable unsafely (as its name implies), this results in arbitrary OS command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid passing any untrusted input as environment variables or arguments to Runtime.exec/ProcessBuilder.",
          "If dynamic behavior is required, use a strict allow-list of expected values and reject anything else.",
          "Do not rely on custom scripts that interpret environment variables as commands; use fixed, parameterized system calls instead.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed command and argument list, and validate/encode any user-supplied values against a strict pattern before use.",
          "Run subprocesses with the minimum privileges necessary and consider sandboxing."
        ]
      }
