        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string data is decoded and passed through an unverified helper (Test.doSomething) then stored directly in the HttpSession without any validation or sanitization appropriate to a trust-boundary crossing (e.g., type/format checks, allow-listing) before being placed into session state.",
        "impact": "Storing unvalidated user input in the session blurs the trust boundary between validated and unvalidated data. Downstream code that reads this session attribute may implicitly trust it as safe/internal data, potentially leading to session poisoning, logic errors, or downstream injection issues if the value is later used in a sensitive context (e.g., authorization decisions, database queries, or unescaped output).",
        "remediation": [
          "Validate and canonicalize the parameter value against a strict allow-list or expected format before storing it in the session.",
          "Avoid storing raw user input in session attributes; store only validated/typed values (e.g., parsed integers, enum values) rather than raw strings.",
          "If the value must be stored, mark it clearly as untrusted and re-validate/re-encode it every time it is read from the session for a specific sink (HTML, SQL, etc.).",
          "Consider using a dedicated DTO/session model with defined validation rules instead of ad-hoc setAttribute calls."
        ]
      }
