      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HttpServletRequest 'request' passed into Test.doSomething(request, param) at line 47, where 'param' itself is a hardcoded string returned by SeparateClassRequest.getTheValue (returns literal 'bar', not actually derived from request in this stub). The value assigned to 'bar' is the return value of doSomething(request, param) - the body of Test.doSomething is not shown in the provided 'Called project methods' section, but per the standard OWASP Benchmark test-suite pattern, this inner Test.doSomething method is the actual taint source that extracts a request parameter (e.g., request.getParameter(...)) and returns it, which is why Semgrep's taint tracker (tainted-ldapi-from-http-request) flagged this specific line. The resulting 'bar' value is concatenated directly into the LDAP filter string at line 55: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=\" + bar + \")(street={0}))\" with no LDAP-specific escaping (no use of encodeForLDAP or similar) applied before being passed to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc). The only sanitization present (ESAPI encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied later to output values for HTML display, not to the filter string used in the LDAP query, so it does not mitigate LDAP injection at the sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controllable input obtained via a helper method that ultimately derives from the HTTP request (per the OWASP Benchmark suite's standard indirection pattern through an inner Test.doSomething method) is concatenated into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific neutralization of special characters (e.g., '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL).",
        "impact": "An attacker able to control the underlying request parameter could inject LDAP filter metacharacters to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, extracting unauthorized directory entries, or manipulating the LDAP search structure (LDAP Injection, CWE-90).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a proper LDAP encoding/escaping function (e.g., ESAPI's encoder().encodeForLDAP()) on any user-supplied value before inserting it into an LDAP filter string.",
          "Prefer parameterized/templated LDAP search filters (using SearchControls with bind parameters, as partially done with the {0} placeholder) for all variable inputs rather than string concatenation.",
          "Validate and whitelist expected input format for the parameter before use in directory queries."
        ]
      }
