      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: cookie value read via request.getCookies() (attacker-controlled HTTP cookie 'BenchmarkTest01850'), URL-decoded into 'param'. This tainted value is passed to doSomething(request, param) and returned as 'bar' (doSomething is a benchmark helper method that simply forwards the tainted string, no sanitization body shown or implied). 'bar' is then concatenated directly into a shell command string: argList.add(\"echo \" + bar), and this list is used to construct and start a ProcessBuilder that invokes 'sh -c' or 'cmd.exe /c' with the tainted command line. No whitelist, escaping, or command-injection-specific sanitization is applied anywhere on this path \u2014 the only downstream processing (Utils.printOSCommandResults) applies HTML encoding to the *output* of the process for XSS protection, which does not mitigate command injection at the point of process creation. Because the cookie value is fully attacker controlled and reaches ProcessBuilder.start() unsanitized, this is exploitable.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied cookie value is decoded and concatenated directly into an OS shell command string without any neutralization of shell metacharacters before being executed via ProcessBuilder with a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c).",
        "impact": "An attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest01850' cookie value can inject arbitrary OS commands or shell metacharacters (e.g., ';', '|', '&&', backticks) that will be executed with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full server compromise, data exfiltration, or further lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with user-controlled input; instead pass command and arguments as separate list elements to ProcessBuilder without shell interpretation.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, strictly validate/whitelist the input against an allow-list of expected values or characters before use.",
          "Use a proper OS command argument escaping library or API designed for the target platform.",
          "Reject or strip any shell metacharacters (;, |, &, $, `, >, <, etc.) from user input before including it in command construction.",
          "Consider using a sandboxed API instead of spawning shell processes altogether."
        ]
      }
    },
