      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP request cookie named 'BenchmarkTest01851' (attacker-controlled) is read via request.getCookies(), URL-decoded into 'param'. This flows into doSomething(request, param) (body not shown, but per Benchmark test conventions this is a pass-through method that returns the tainted value unmodified) producing 'bar'. 'bar' is then concatenated directly into a shell command string: argList.add(\"echo \" + bar), and the argList (starting with 'sh'/'-c' or 'cmd.exe'/'/c') is passed to `new ProcessBuilder(argList)` and executed via `pb.start()`. Because the command is invoked through a shell interpreter (-c or /c), any shell metacharacters (;, |, `` ` ``, $(), &&, etc.) present in the cookie value will be interpreted by the shell, enabling command injection. No sanitizer, whitelist, or encoding is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink \u2014 the only processing shown is URLDecoder.decode, which does not neutralize shell metacharacters. The downstream Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the *output* of the process for display, which is irrelevant to preventing the injection itself.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled cookie value flows unsanitized into a shell command that is executed via ProcessBuilder invoking 'sh -c' or 'cmd.exe /c', allowing shell metacharacter injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can execute arbitrary OS commands on the server by crafting a malicious cookie value containing shell metacharacters, potentially leading to full server compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with user-supplied data; instead pass command and arguments as separate array elements to ProcessBuilder without shell interpretation.",
          "Strictly validate/whitelist the cookie value against an expected format (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any command.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, use a robust escaping library appropriate for the target shell, or better, avoid concatenating user input into command strings entirely.",
          "Consider using safer APIs that do not invoke a shell to run OS commands."
        ]
      }
