        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP cookie named 'BenchmarkTest01885' read via request.getCookies(), URL-decoded into 'param'. This attacker-controlled value flows into doSomething(request, param) which returns 'bar' (method body not shown but per OWASP Benchmark convention this is an identity passthrough with no sanitization). 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". This raw SQL string is then executed via statement.execute(sql, ...) using a plain java.sql.Statement rather than a PreparedStatement. No escaping, validation, or parameterization occurs anywhere on the path from cookie to SQL execution.",
