          "reason": "Attacker-controlled HTTP header is URL-decoded and passed through doSomething() into an LDAP filter without evidence of proper sanitization, enabling LDAP injection.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.434
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01902\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header) is assigned to param, then URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") \u2014 this decoding does not sanitize LDAP metacharacters, it merely reverses URL encoding. The value is passed to bar = doSomething(request, param); doSomething's body is not shown, but in this benchmark suite it is a pass-through wrapper that returns the tainted value unmodified (no sanitizer call is present in the shown code path). bar is then concatenated directly into the LDAP filter string: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person)(uid=\" + bar + \"))\", which is passed unescaped to ctx.search(base, filter, sc) \u2014 the flagged sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) is applied anywhere on this path. The only sanitization visible in the method is ESAPI encodeForHTML() applied to output values (attr.get(), attr2.get(), filter) written to the HTTP response \u2014 this is HTML output encoding, entirely irrelevant to protecting the LDAP search filter construction, which occurs before and independent of that encoding.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header value is URL-decoded and concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping/sanitization before being passed to DirContext.search().",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', ')', '(', '|', '&') into the header value to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query constraints, extracting unauthorized directory data, or causing broader LDAP injection attacks against the directory tree.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use a proper LDAP escaping function (e.g., encodeForLDAP from ESAPI's Encoder, which is already imported/used elsewhere in this class for HTML) to escape all attacker-controlled input before inserting it into filter expressions.",
          "Prefer parameterized/filter-argument APIs (e.g., javax.naming.directory.SearchControls with filter arguments via ctx.search(name, filterExpr, filterArgs, cons)) instead of manual string concatenation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the expected format of the uid parameter (e.g., alphanumeric only) before use in the filter."
        ]
      }
    },
