      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: the HTTP 'Referer' request header (attacker/client-controllable). It is URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode and assigned to 'param', then passed into doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown in this context (helper not provided). The result 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and written directly via response.getWriter().format(\"Formatted like: %1$s and %2$s.\", obj) \u2014 the Writer.format() call performs no HTML entity encoding whatsoever, it is a raw output stream sink. No encoder, escaper, or validator is visible anywhere on this path in the shown code. Given the OWASP Benchmark test pattern (doSomething typically acts as an identity/pass-through wrapper in this suite unless it explicitly implements a validator), and given no sanitization logic appears between the header read and the write, the tainted value reaches an XSS-sensitive sink unescaped.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled data from the Referer HTTP header is decoded and written directly to the response body using an unescaped Writer.format() call, bypassing any HTML-context output encoding.",
        "impact": "An attacker who can influence the Referer header sent to the vulnerable endpoint (e.g., via a crafted link, meta-refresh, or intermediary redirect) could inject HTML/JavaScript that gets reflected unescaped into the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting and potential session/token theft or UI redress in the victim's browser.",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode/escape the value before writing it to the response (e.g., use OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() on 'bar' before formatting).",
          "Avoid writing directly via response.getWriter(); use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Do not trust the Referer header for reflecting content back to the client; validate/allow-list expected values if it must be used.",
          "Set a strict Content-Security-Policy to mitigate impact of any residual XSS."
        ]
      }
