        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"Referer\") (attacker-controlled HTTP header) is read into 'param' at lines 44-46, then URL-decoded (line 49) which does not neutralize HTML/JS metacharacters. The value is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose implementation is not shown, but in this test-suite pattern such helper methods are typically pass-through/no-op transformations. The result 'bar' is then written directly to the client via response.getWriter().println(bar) at line 54 with no HTML-encoding, escaping, or use of a templating/view layer. Content-Type is text/html, so any HTML/script in the Referer header will be reflected verbatim in the response body. No sanitizer or encoder (e.g., ESAPI, OWASP Encoder, JSTL c:out) is applied on this path.",
