        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "Untrusted HTTP header value flows unsanitized into a shell command string ('echo ' + bar) executed via ProcessBuilder with 'sh -c'/'cmd.exe /c', allowing shell metacharacter injection since no validation/whitelisting/escaping is performed on the value before it is embedded in the command.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands via the BenchmarkTest01928 HTTP header, leading to arbitrary command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process, potentially resulting in full system compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c/cmd.exe /c) with user-controlled input; if command execution is required, invoke the target binary directly with an argument array (no shell interpretation).",
          "Validate the header value against a strict allow-list of expected characters/values before use.",
          "If shell invocation cannot be avoided, properly escape/quote the value for the specific shell, or reject input containing shell metacharacters (;, |, &, `, $, (), etc.).",
          "Consider using safer APIs (e.g., Java's ProcessBuilder without a shell wrapper) and passing arguments as separate list elements rather than concatenated strings."
