        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands or command arguments via the 'BenchmarkTest01942' HTTP header, leading to arbitrary command execution on the server with the privileges of the web application process, potentially resulting in full system compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid building shell command strings from user input; use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and an argument list instead of concatenating strings passed to Runtime.exec.",
          "If OS command execution with dynamic input is unavoidable, validate the input against a strict allow-list of expected values (e.g., a fixed set of command names/arguments) and reject anything else.",
          "Do not rely on URL-decoding as a security control; apply proper escaping/quoting appropriate for the target OS shell, or better, avoid the shell entirely.",
          "Run the external process with the least privileges necessary and consider sandboxing to limit impact if injection occurs."
        ]
      }
