      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01958\") is attacker-controlled HTTP header. It is URL-decoded and passed to doSomething(request, param), whose return value 'bar' is put directly into the HTTP session via request.getSession().putValue(\"userid\", bar) at line 54. No sanitization/validation is applied to 'bar' before it is stored in the session \u2014 the only encoding (Utils.encodeForHTML) is applied afterward, only for the HTML output written to the response, not for the session attribute itself. Thus, untrusted header-derived data crosses into the trusted session store unsanitized, matching the exact pattern flagged by the tainted-session-from-http-request rule.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "low"
      }
