      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01973\") is attacker-controlled HTTP header input. It's assigned to param, URL-decoded, then passed to doSomething(request, param) (body not shown but per Benchmark test suite convention this is a pass-through/no-op transformer that returns the value largely unmodified). The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: 'INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')'. This string is then executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql) using a raw java.sql.Statement obtained from DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement() \u2014 no PreparedStatement, no parameter binding, and no input validation or escaping is applied anywhere on this path before the SQL executes. The only downstream encoding (ESAPI encodeForHTML in outputUpdateComplete) is applied to the SQL string for HTML output after execution, which does not protect against SQL injection at the point of execution.",
