        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled header value is concatenated directly into a SQL statement string without parameterization or sanitization, then executed via Statement.executeUpdate.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the BenchmarkTest01973 HTTP header, potentially allowing unauthorized data modification, extraction, or destruction in the users table or beyond, depending on DB permissions.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use PreparedStatement with parameterized queries instead of building SQL via string concatenation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the header value format before use if it must remain part of dynamic logic.",
          "Apply least-privilege database credentials to limit blast radius of injection.",
          "Ensure any helper transformation (doSomething) performs actual sanitization/encoding appropriate for SQL context, not just pass-through logic."
        ]
