        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeader(\"BenchmarkTest01973\") is fully attacker-controlled (an HTTP header). Value is URL-decoded and passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body isn't shown, but the OWASP Benchmark helper pattern for these methods simply returns the tainted parameter unchanged (no sanitization is applied elsewhere in the visible flow). The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: 'INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES (\\'foo\\',\\'' + bar + '\\')' with no escaping/parameterization, then executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement rather than a PreparedStatement. No validator, allow-list, or SQL-specific encoder is applied on this path \u2014 the only encoding downstream is ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(sql) in outputUpdateComplete, which is applied AFTER the query has already executed and is for HTML output, not SQL escaping, so it does not mitigate the injection.",
