        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled input from an HTTP header is URL-decoded and passed through an unverified helper method directly into a java.io.File constructor without canonicalization, whitelisting, or rejection of '../' traversal sequences before being used in a filesystem operation (exists()).",
        "impact": "An attacker can supply a header value containing directory traversal sequences (e.g., '../../etc/passwd') to make the application check for the existence of arbitrary files outside the intended directory, resulting in information disclosure about the filesystem's structure/contents (existence of arbitrary paths), and potentially enabling further attacks if the file path is later used for read/write operations.",
