        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02036\") returns attacker-controlled HTTP header value, assigned to 'param'. This value is URL-decoded (URLDecoder.decode) then passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but is a benchmark helper that returns the value largely unchanged (no LDAP-specific escaping is indicated anywhere in the visible code or provided helper methods). The result 'bar' is directly string-concatenated into the LDAP filter: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))'. This filter string is passed as the raw filter argument to idc.search(base, filter, filters, sc). Only the 'street' portion uses a safe parameterized substitution ({0} with the filters array); the 'uid=' portion embeds the tainted value via direct string concatenation, which is not neutralized before reaching the LDAP search sink. No LDAP-specific encoding/escaping (e.g., escaping of *()\\NUL characters) is applied to 'bar' at any point on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header data is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without LDAP-specific escaping/sanitization before being passed to DirContext.search().",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', ')', '(', '|', '&') via the HTTP header to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing authentication/authorization checks, extracting unauthorized directory data, or enumerating LDAP tree entries (LDAP injection, CWE-90).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized LDAP search filters (e.g., pass all variable values via the 'filters' Object[] array with {n} placeholders) instead of concatenating tainted input directly into the filter string.",
          "Apply proper LDAP filter encoding (e.g., ESAPI's encodeForLDAP or similar) to any user-supplied value before inserting it into a filter string.",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected format of the header value (e.g., restrict to alphanumeric characters) before use in the LDAP query."
        ]
      }
    },
