      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02037\") reads an attacker-controlled HTTP header value into 'param'. This is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) preserving attacker control, then passed to doSomething(request, param) which returns 'bar' (body not shown, but per Benchmark test conventions this is a pass-through wrapper that does not sanitize LDAP metacharacters). 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the LDAP filter string: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))' with no escaping of LDAP special characters (parentheses, asterisks, backslashes, NUL). This filter is passed to idc.search(base, filter, filters, sc), the flagged sink (javax.naming.directory.InitialDirContext.search). The only sanitization visible in the method is ESAPI encodeForHTML() applied to output values written to the HTTP response (attr.get(), attr2.get(), and the filter string in the 'not found' branch) \u2014 this is HTML output encoding, which does not neutralize LDAP filter metacharacters and is applied only for display, not before the search call. Therefore no adequate LDAP-specific sanitizer/encoder is applied on the path from header input to the search sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header value is URL-decoded and concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without escaping LDAP special characters (e.g., via javax.naming.ldap or manual escaping of parentheses/asterisks/backslashes) before being passed to DirContext.search().",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters via the HTTP header to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, extracting unauthorized directory data, or manipulating LDAP tree searches (LDAP injection).",
        "remediation": [
          "Escape LDAP special characters (\\, *, (, ), NUL) in user input before building the filter string, e.g., using a dedicated LDAP encoding utility (such as ESAPI's encodeForLDAP or Java's javax.naming.ldap escaping helpers).",
          "Prefer parameterized LDAP filters (using the {0} substitution mechanism already used for 'street') for all user-controlled filter components instead of string concatenation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the expected format of the header value before use in any query context."
        ]
      }
    },
