      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") - user-controlled HTTP header. It is captured into 'param', URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode (which does not perform HTML/JS encoding), then passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but per its naming and typical Benchmark helper pattern is a pass-through/data-shuffling function with no HTML sanitization. The result 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and written via out.format(...) directly to the raw PrintWriter obtained from response.getWriter(), bypassing any templating/escaping layer. No encoding (e.g., ESAPI encoder, StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml, JSTL c:out) is applied anywhere on this path before the sink.",
