        "impact": "An attacker who can control or spoof the Referer header (e.g., via a crafted link, XHR, or intermediate proxy) can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript that will be reflected verbatim in the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) that can lead to session hijacking, credential theft, or arbitrary actions in the victim's browser context.",
