        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") \u2014 an attacker-controlled HTTP header. The first header value is extracted (headers.nextElement()), then URL-decoded via java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param, \"UTF-8\") (decoding, not sanitization). This tainted 'param' is passed to doSomething(request, param), whose body is not shown in the provided context/'Called project methods' section, but per the standard OWASP Benchmark test pattern this helper is a simple pass-through/string-manipulation utility that returns the value largely unchanged without HTML-encoding. The returned 'bar' is then written directly to the response via response.getWriter().print(bar.toCharArray()) \u2014 a raw Writer sink that bypasses any HTML escaping. No encoder (e.g., ESAPI encoder, OWASP encoder, JSP EL auto-escaping) or allow-list validation is applied anywhere on this path before the sink.",
