        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled Referer header value is decoded and forwarded through a helper method to a raw output writer without any HTML/context-appropriate output encoding or input validation, allowing injected markup/script to be reflected in the response.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a request with a malicious Referer header (feasible via a redirect page, meta-refresh, or a controlled referring page) causing arbitrary HTML/JavaScript to be reflected in the response, leading to reflected Cross-Site Scripting (session hijacking, credential theft, defacement, etc.).",
        "remediation": [
          "Encode all user-derived data before writing to the response using a context-aware encoder (e.g., OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) rather than writing raw bytes/chars via getWriter().print().",
          "Avoid writing directly to the OutputStream/Writer for dynamic content; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Do not trust the Referer header for reflection into HTML output; if it must be displayed, HTML-encode it just before insertion.",
          "Add explicit output encoding inside doSomething() or immediately before the print() call, and add a regression test verifying `<script>` payloads in the Referer header are neutralized."
        ]
