          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User input from Referer header is decoded and passed through doSomething() then written directly to response via printf without HTML escaping, creating a direct XSS vector.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.23
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"Referer\") header value is grabbed (attacker-controlled, e.g. crafted by an attacker who can control redirects/links causing the victim's browser to send a spoofed Referer, or via any HTTP client). It is URL-decoded and passed as 'param' into doSomething(request, param); the body of doSomething is not shown in this context, but nothing in the visible code applies any HTML/JS output encoding or validation before or after this call. The returned value 'bar' is inserted directly into an Object[] and written via response.getWriter().printf(...) \u2014 a raw Writer sink that bypasses any templating/escaping layer, matching the CWE-79 no-direct-response-writer rule. No encodeForHTML/ESAPI/StringEscapeUtils or similar sanitizer is applied anywhere on this path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP Referer header is decoded and, absent any shown sanitization in doSomething, written unescaped straight into the HTTP response body via getWriter().printf, allowing injected HTML/JS to be reflected to the browser.",
        "impact": "An attacker who can influence the Referer header seen by the server (e.g., via a crafted link, a controlled redirecting page, or direct HTTP request in contexts where Referer is attacker-controlled) can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript that executes in the context of the victim's browser session, leading to reflected Cross-Site Scripting (session hijacking, credential theft, defacement, etc.).",
        "remediation": [
          "HTML-encode/escape all dynamic values before writing them via the raw response Writer (e.g., using OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml() or ESAPI's encodeForHTML).",
          "Avoid writing directly to the response Writer/OutputStream for dynamic content; use a templating engine (JSP/JSF) that auto-escapes output.",
          "Validate/allow-list the Referer header value if it must be reflected, rejecting or stripping any HTML meta-characters.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers as defense-in-depth against reflected XSS."
        ]
      }
    },
