        "impact": "An attacker can craft a malicious Referer header (e.g., via a crafted link, CSRF-triggered request, or a controlled referring page) containing HTML/JavaScript payloads that get reflected unescaped in the response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) able to execute arbitrary script in the victim's browser session, leading to session hijacking, credential theft, or defacement.",
