          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.446
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: the HTTP 'Referer' request header (attacker-controlled) is read via request.getHeaders(\"Referer\"), URL-decoded with java.net.URLDecoder.decode (which only reverses percent-encoding, providing no HTML/XSS sanitization), then passed into doSomething(request, param) to produce 'bar'. 'bar' is then used directly as the format string in response.getWriter().printf(bar, obj) \u2014 writing raw, potentially malicious content into the HTTP response body without any HTML encoding. No output encoder or contextual sanitizer is applied at any point along this path, and printf() does not perform HTML escaping. The doSomething() helper body is not shown, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite these are typically simple pass-through/transform methods with no XSS-specific sanitization; nothing in the visible code neutralizes the payload before it reaches the writer sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled data from the Referer HTTP header is URL-decoded (which does not neutralize HTML/JS metacharacters) and written directly to the response output stream via getWriter().printf() without any HTML/XSS output encoding.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a malicious Referer header containing HTML/JavaScript payloads that, when reflected unescaped in the response, could execute in a victim's browser (reflected Cross-Site Scripting), leading to session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid writing user-controlled data directly via response.getWriter(); use a view/templating layer that performs contextual output encoding (e.g., JSP with auto-escaping, JSF, or OWASP Java Encoder).",
          "Explicitly HTML-encode any user-supplied header values before including them in the response body (e.g., using OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()).",
          "Do not use raw user input as a printf format string or argument written to the response stream.",
          "Set appropriate Content-Security-Policy headers to reduce the impact of any residual XSS."
        ]
      }
    },
