      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02059\") returns an attacker-controlled HTTP header value, assigned to 'param'. This is URL-decoded and passed to doSomething(request, param); doSomething's body is not shown, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite these helper wrappers are pass-through utilities that do not sanitize the value, so 'bar' retains attacker control. 'bar' is then concatenated into \"echo \" + bar and placed as the third element of the args array passed to `new ProcessBuilder(args)`, which is executed via pb.start(). Because a1/a2 are 'sh'/'-c' or 'cmd.exe'/'/c', the third argument is interpreted by the shell as a full command line, so shell metacharacters (e.g., ';', '|', '&&') in the header value would be interpreted, enabling command injection. No sanitizer, allow-list, or escaping is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink; the only processing shown is URL-decoding, which does not neutralize shell metacharacters.",
