        "impact": "An attacker who controls the 'BenchmarkTest02059' HTTP header can inject arbitrary OS commands executed with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full server compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with concatenated user input; use ProcessBuilder with a fixed executable and pass arguments as separate array elements without shell interpretation.",
          "Strictly validate/allow-list the header value against expected characters (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any command.",
          "If shell execution is unavoidable, use a robust escaping/quoting library appropriate for the target OS shell.",
          "Apply the principle of least privilege to the process executing the command to limit blast radius if injection occurs."
