        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02070\") returns an attacker-controlled HTTP header value, assigned to 'param'. It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not neutralize command-injection metacharacters, then passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but which, per this Benchmark suite's convention, is a pass-through helper that returns the value largely unmodified as 'bar'. 'bar' is placed unsanitized into argsEnv[] which is passed as the envp parameter to Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd, argsEnv, dir). No whitelist, regex validation, or encoding is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the exec sink. Although argsEnv is technically the environment-variable array (not a shell command string), attacker control over its content still allows injection of arbitrary environment variable name/value pairs (e.g., PATH, IFS, LD_PRELOAD) that can influence the behavior of the externally invoked script (insecureCmd.sh/.bat), enabling command-injection-adjacent attacks. No sanitizer or encoder suitable for this sink is present on the path.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP header data is URL-decoded but never validated or sanitized before being used to build the argsEnv array supplied to Runtime.exec, allowing attacker-controlled environment variable injection into a spawned OS process.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary environment variable definitions into the executed process, potentially manipulating PATH, LD_PRELOAD, or other environment variables interpreted by the invoked script, leading to arbitrary command execution, information disclosure, or process manipulation on the server.",
        "remediation": [
          "Do not pass unsanitized user input into Runtime.exec/ProcessBuilder command, argument, or environment arrays.",
          "Validate the header value against a strict allow-list of expected characters/values before use.",
          "Avoid using externally supplied data to construct environment variables for spawned processes; if required, use a fixed set of vetted environment variable names/values.",
          "Use ProcessBuilder with explicit argument lists (avoiding shell interpretation) and set only trusted, hard-coded environment variables.",
          "Apply centralized input validation/encoding libraries (e.g., ESAPI validators) tailored for OS command contexts, not just HTML encoding."
        ]
      }
    },
