      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02093\") retrieves an attacker-controlled HTTP header value. It is URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode, then passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but per Benchmark test conventions is a pass-through that returns the tainted value unchanged. The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"...PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" without any escaping, parameterization, or validation. This raw sql string is then executed via statement.execute(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement (not PreparedStatement). No sanitizer, allow-list validator, or query parameterization exists on this path before the sink.",
