        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02094\") returns an attacker-controlled HTTP header value, captured into 'param'. It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not sanitize for SQL context, then passed through doSomething(request, param) into 'bar' (body not shown, but Benchmark's doSomething helpers are typically simple pass-through/transform methods that do not perform SQL-specific sanitization). 'bar' is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"... PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\" forming 'sql'. This string is then executed via statement.execute(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement obtained from DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement() \u2014 no PreparedStatement, no parameterization, and no escaping/validation is applied to 'bar' anywhere in the shown code path. This is a textbook SQL injection sink for a header-derived value.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP header value is URL-decoded and directly concatenated into a SQL query string, which is then executed via Statement.execute() without using a parameterized/prepared statement or any input validation/escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a malicious HTTP header value to inject arbitrary SQL, potentially bypassing authentication, exfiltrating or modifying data, or in some database configurations executing further destructive operations.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use java.sql.PreparedStatement with parameterized queries instead of building SQL via string concatenation.",
          "Bind the header-derived value as a parameter (e.g., ps.setString(1, bar)) rather than interpolating it into the SQL text.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the header value if it represents a bounded set of expected values.",
          "Avoid trusting HTTP headers as safe input; treat them the same as any other untrusted user input."
        ]
      }
    },
