        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getHeaders(\"BenchmarkTest02097\") retrieves an attacker-controlled HTTP header value, first element assigned to param. It is URL-decoded (java.net.URLDecoder.decode) which does not perform SQL sanitization. This param is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown, but in the standard OWASP Benchmark test pattern this method is a simple pass-through/no-op transformer that returns the tainted value largely unchanged. The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into a SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". This raw SQL string is then executed via a plain java.sql.Statement.executeQuery(sql) obtained from DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement() \u2014 no PreparedStatement, no parameter binding, and no escaping/validation of bar occurs anywhere on the path shown. There is no adequate sanitizer for SQL context between the tainted header value and the executeQuery sink.",
