      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02104\") assigned to 'param' (attacker-controlled, defaults to empty string if null but otherwise fully controlled). This flows into doSomething(request, param) whose body isn't shown here but is a pass-through helper per Benchmark test conventions; its result is assigned to 'bar'. 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the LDAP search filter string: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=\" + bar + \")(street={0}))\". This filter is passed unmodified to ctx.search(base, filter, filters, sc) \u2014 the flagged sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., escaping of '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', NUL) is applied to 'bar' before it is embedded in the filter. The only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later to output values (attr.get(), attr2.get(), filter) for HTML display, not to the raw filter construction \u2014 that encoding is irrelevant to the LDAP injection risk since it happens after the query has already executed. The '{0}' placeholder mechanism, which could have safely parameterized untrusted input, is unused for 'bar' and only used for the unrelated 'street' constant. Thus, an attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters via the BenchmarkTest02104 parameter to alter the search filter logic (e.g., closing the uid clause early or injecting additional filter clauses), constituting a genuine LDAP injection.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific escaping or use of the available parameterized substitution mechanism ({0}), allowing filter syntax injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the LDAP query logic to bypass intended search constraints, extract unauthorized directory data, or in some LDAP configurations affect directory tree operations, leading to information disclosure or logic bypass in directory-based authentication/authorization systems.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use the JNDI DirContext.search overload with parameterized filter arguments (the {0}, {1} placeholders) for ALL untrusted values, not just constants \u2014 pass 'bar' via the filters Object[] array instead of concatenating it into the filter string.",
          "Apply LDAP-specific escaping to user input before building filter strings (escape '(', ')', '*', '\\\\', and NUL characters per RFC 4515), e.g. using ESAPI's encodeForLDAP or an equivalent library function.",
          "Validate/allow-list the expected format of the BenchmarkTest02104 parameter (e.g., restrict to alphanumeric characters) before use in the LDAP filter."
        ]
      }
    },
