        "impact": "An attacker could supply a value like '../../etc/passwd' or similar traversal sequences to make the application check for (and disclose via the exists()/does not exist branch) the presence of arbitrary files outside the intended TESTFILES_DIR, resulting in information disclosure about the filesystem structure, and potentially worse if the file object were later used for read/write operations.",
        "remediation": [
          "Canonicalize the resulting File path (File.getCanonicalPath()) and verify it still resides within the intended base directory (Utils.TESTFILES_DIR) before use.",
          "Use org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(...) or similar to strip any directory components from the user-supplied parameter before constructing the File object.",
          "Reject or sanitize input containing '..' or path separator characters before using it in file path construction.",
          "Employ a whitelist of allowed filenames instead of accepting arbitrary user input for file paths."
        ]
      }
