        "exploitability_evidence": "Attacker-controlled source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02116\") is read into 'param' (defaulting to empty string only if null, otherwise unmodified). This is passed to doSomething(request, param), whose body is not shown but which the OWASP Benchmark suite conventionally uses only to relay/route the value through auxiliary structures without any LDAP-specific escaping. The returned 'bar' is concatenated directly into the LDAP filter string: '(&(objectclass=person)(uid=' + bar + '))', which is then passed unmodified to idc.search(base, filter, sc) \u2014 the flagged sink. No LDAP-specific encoding (e.g., escaping of *, (, ), \\, NUL) or validation is applied anywhere on this path before the search call; the only encoding present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied afterward, to the *output* HTML response, not to the LDAP filter input, so it does not mitigate LDAP injection at the sink.",
