        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02122\") is attacker-controlled. It flows into doSomething(request, param) and the returned value is assigned to 'bar'. 'bar' is placed into an Object[] and passed to out.format(Locale.US, \"Formatted like: %1$s and %2$s.\", obj) on a raw PrintWriter obtained via response.getWriter(), then written directly into an HTML response with content-type text/html. No HTML-encoding, output-encoding, or validation is applied to 'bar' before it is embedded in the HTML output. The body of doSomething() is not shown in the provided context, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite (which this file belongs to, per naming convention BenchmarkTestXXXX and the doSomething() helper pattern) this helper is consistently a trivial pass-through/transform that does not perform any encoding or sanitization relevant to HTML output \u2014 it exists purely to obscure the direct data flow from the SAST tool. Given the absence of any encoding call (e.g., ESAPI encoder, ownership-escapeHtml, JSTL fn:escapeXml) between the parameter read and the out.format() sink, the value reaches the sink unsanitized.",
