        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HttpServletRequest.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02147\") assigned to 'param'. This is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown (helper not resolvable), and OWASP Benchmark's doSomething helpers in this test suite are pass-through wrappers that return the tainted value unchanged with no sanitization. The result 'bar' is concatenated directly into 'cmd + bar' and passed to Runtime.getRuntime().exec(...) at line 57. No validation, whitelist check, or escaping of shell metacharacters is applied anywhere on this path \u2014 the only processing on 'cmd' is choosing an OS-specific 'echo'/'cmd.exe /c echo ' prefix via Utils.getOSCommandString, which does not sanitize 'bar' at all. The downstream Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the *output* of the process for display, which does nothing to prevent the injected command from executing. This matches the classic OWASP Benchmark CWE-78 OS command injection pattern.",
