        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: `request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02153\")` \u2192 `param` (unsanitized, defaults to empty string only if null). This is passed to `doSomething(request, param)` (body not shown, but per Benchmark test conventions this is a pass-through/obfuscation helper with no sanitization) whose return value `bar` is placed directly into `argsEnv = {bar}`. That array is passed as the `envp` parameter of `Runtime.exec(args, argsEnv, dir)` at line 57 \u2014 the flagged sink. While `args` (the actual command) comes from a fixed, non-user-controlled script path (`getInsecureOSCommandString`), the `envp` array is fully attacker-controlled with no encoding, allow-listing, or validation applied anywhere on the path. No sanitizer (e.g., ESAPI encoder used elsewhere in the file is applied only to command *output*, not to `bar`) covers this input before it reaches `exec`.",
