        "remediation": [
          "Use PreparedStatement / parameterized queries with bind variables instead of string concatenation for the SQL WHERE clause.",
          "If using Spring JdbcTemplate, use the query methods that accept SQL with '?' placeholders and pass parameters separately (queryForList(sql, params...)) rather than building the SQL string manually.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the parameter if it must remain part of dynamic query construction.",
          "Avoid returning raw SQL error text to the client; keep the hideSQLErrors safeguard but ensure it defaults to true in production."
        ]
      }
