        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02187\") assigned to param (defaults to \"\" if null). This is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown, but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper is a pass-through/no-op that returns the tainted value unchanged, assigning it to bar. bar is directly concatenated into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". This string is then executed via statement.execute(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement (obtained via DatabaseHelper.getSqlStatement()), not a PreparedStatement. No sanitization, escaping, or parameterization is applied to bar before it reaches the SQL execution sink.",
