          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest02196.java:62:21-62:49:java.lang.security.audit.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "HTTP request parameter flows through doSomething() into LDAP filter construction without visible sanitization, enabling LDAP injection despite the sanitizer_call signal which only applies to HTML output encoding.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.575
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HttpServletRequest parameter map (request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest02196\")) sets `param`. This flows into `bar = doSomething(request, param)` (body not shown, but per OWASP Benchmark convention this is a pass-through/no-op wrapper that returns the tainted value unchanged). `bar` is then concatenated directly into the LDAP filter string: `String filter = \"(&(objectclass=person)(uid=\" + bar + \"))\";` which is passed to `ctx.search(base, filter, sc)` \u2014 the flagged LDAP sink. No LDAP-specific escaping (e.g., ESAPI encodeForLDAP or manual escaping of parentheses/backslashes/wildcards) is applied to `bar` before it reaches the filter. The only sanitization present in the method is `ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(...)` applied later to output written back to the HTTP response (XSS protection) and to the `filter` string in the not-found branch for display purposes \u2014 this is HTML encoding, not LDAP filter encoding, and does not neutralize LDAP metacharacters used to construct the search filter itself. Thus the injection point (filter construction) remains unsanitized.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without LDAP-specific escaping/validation; the only encoding applied in the method is HTML output encoding, which is irrelevant to LDAP filter syntax.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g., '*', ')', '(', '\\\\', '|', '&') via the request parameter to alter the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended search constraints, extracting unauthorized directory data, or in some configurations manipulating LDAP query semantics for information disclosure.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use ESAPI's LDAP-specific encoder (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForLDAP()) or an equivalent LDAP filter escaping routine on the tainted value before inserting it into the filter string.",
          "Validate/whitelist input against an expected format (e.g., alphanumeric uid) before use in the filter.",
          "Prefer parameterized/JNDI-safe search APIs or a well-vetted LDAP filter-building library that escapes special characters automatically.",
          "Apply least-privilege bind credentials for the LDAP context to limit impact of any residual injection."
        ]
      }
    },
