        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest02203\")[0] is fully attacker-controlled and assigned to 'param'. It is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown but is the standard OWASP Benchmark pass-through helper that returns the parameter unmodified (as evidenced by no sanitizer being applied elsewhere on this value). The returned 'bar' is concatenated directly into fileName = TESTFILES_DIR + bar with no path normalization, validation, or filename-only extraction (e.g., FilenameUtils.getName is not used). This fileName is then used to construct 'new java.io.File(fileName)' and opened via FileOutputStream at line 71 (the flagged sink), allowing '../' sequences to escape the intended directory. The only encoding present, ESAPI encoder().encodeForHTML(fileName), is applied solely to the string printed back to the HTTP response for display purposes and does not sanitize or restrict the path used for the actual file write operation. Therefore no sanitizer relevant to CWE-22 protects the sink.",
