        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() extracts the 'BenchmarkTest02208' HTTP parameter into 'param'. This is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown, but per standard OWASP Benchmark test conventions, doSomething() is a pass-through helper that returns the tainted value unmodified (it does not appear in the 'Called project methods' section, implying no sanitization logic exists there). The result 'bar' is directly concatenated into the LDAP filter string: '(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=' + bar + ')(street={0}))' without any escaping of LDAP special characters (e.g., '(', ')', '*', '\\', NUL). The filter is then passed to idc.search(base, filter, filters, sc). Note the filters array only binds a placeholder {0} for the 'street' attribute \u2014 the 'uid' portion containing 'bar' is raw string concatenation, not parameterized. No LDAP-specific encoder (e.g., ESAPI encodeForLDAP) is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the sink; the only ESAPI encoding calls (encodeForHTML) occur later on output to the HTTP response, which is irrelevant to the LDAP injection sink.",
