      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest02244\")[0] is fully attacker-controlled HTTP parameter data, assigned to 'param'. This flows into 'bar = doSomething(request, param)' \u2014 the doSomething helper's body isn't shown, but in this codebase pattern it is a pass-through/transform that does not sanitize for shell metacharacters (no sanitizer is shown or referenced anywhere on this path). 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the command string \"echo \" + bar and added to argList, which is executed via 'sh -c' or 'cmd.exe /c' through ProcessBuilder.start(). No whitelist, escaping, or shell-metacharacter filtering is applied to bar before it reaches the ProcessBuilder sink. The only sanitization present (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML in Utils.printOSCommandResults) is applied to command *output* for HTML display, not to the command *input* before execution \u2014 irrelevant to the OS command injection sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated unsanitized into a shell command string ('echo ' + bar) that is executed via ProcessBuilder using a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c), allowing injection of arbitrary shell metacharacters (e.g., ;, |, `` ` ``, $()) since no validation, escaping, or whitelisting occurs on the tainted value before it reaches the exec sink.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands executed with the privileges of the web application process, potentially leading to full server compromise, data exfiltration, or lateral movement.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with concatenated user input; instead pass command and arguments as separate list elements to ProcessBuilder without shell interpretation.",
          "Validate/whitelist the parameter value against a strict allow-list of expected values before use.",
          "If shell invocation is unavoidable, use a robust escaping library appropriate for the target OS shell, or reject any input containing shell metacharacters.",
          "Run the subprocess with the least privileges necessary and consider sandboxing."
        ]
      }
    },
