        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() -> param (attacker-controlled HTTP parameter 'BenchmarkTest02249'). This raw param is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose result is stored in bar; the body of doSomething is not shown but per the Benchmark test suite convention it acts as a pass-through/taint-propagator that returns the tainted string unmodified. bar is then concatenated directly with cmd (a fixed OS-command prefix from Utils.getOSCommandString, e.g. 'cmd.exe /c echo ' or 'echo ') and passed straight into Runtime.exec(cmd + bar) at line 61. No validation, whitelist check, or shell-metacharacter encoding is applied to bar before it reaches exec. The only sanitizer visible in the file (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is used later on the *output* of the process (in printOSCommandResults and in the exception handler) \u2014 that only protects the HTTP response from XSS, it does not sanitize the command string used to build the OS command, so it is irrelevant to this CWE-78 sink.",
