        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() extracts a value keyed by 'BenchmarkTest02250' into 'param' (attacker-controlled). This flows into 'bar = doSomething(request, param)' \u2014 doSomething's body is not shown, but no sanitizer/validator is applied to it in the visible code path. 'cmd' is built from a hardcoded string 'echo' via Utils.getOSCommandString (not tainted). The sink is 'r.exec(cmd + bar)' at line 61, directly concatenating the tainted 'bar' into the OS command with no whitelist/escaping. The only sanitization visible in this method (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied to the exception message for HTML output in the catch block \u2014 it is irrelevant to the exec() sink and provides no protection against command injection.",
