        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap().get(\"BenchmarkTest02273\")[0] is fully attacker-controlled HTTP parameter data. It is assigned to 'param', then passed through 'bar = doSomething(request, param)' (body not shown/available, and in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper is a pass-through/no-op that does not perform SQL-specific sanitization). The tainted 'bar' is then directly concatenated into a raw SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". This raw, unparameterized SQL string is passed straight to org.owasp.benchmark.helpers.DatabaseHelper.JDBCtemplate.batchUpdate(sql), which executes it as a SQL statement. The only encoding applied (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(sql)) is applied afterward to the string for HTML output purposes only \u2014 it does not sanitize the value before it reaches the SQL sink, and HTML encoding is not an adequate SQL sanitizer regardless. No parameterized query, prepared statement, or SQL-specific escaping/validation is applied anywhere on the path from source to sink.",
