        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries / PreparedStatement with bind variables instead of string concatenation for the SQL command.",
          "If using Spring JdbcTemplate, use the overload accepting a SQL string with parameter placeholders and an argument array rather than building the SQL by concatenation.",
          "Apply strict allow-list input validation on the parameter value if it must be used in a dynamic query context.",
          "Do not rely on HTML encoding (ESAPI encodeForHTML) as a defense against SQL injection \u2014 it is irrelevant to the SQL sink."
        ]
