        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterMap() extracts the 'BenchmarkTest02285' parameter value into 'param' (attacker-controlled HTTP request parameter). This value is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown, but in this OWASP Benchmark test suite pattern such helper methods perform trivial pass-through/no-op transformations and do not sanitize for SQL. The result 'bar' is concatenated directly into the SQL string: \"SELECT * from USERS where USERNAME='foo' and PASSWORD='\" + bar + \"'\". This concatenated string is then passed to statement.execute(sql, ...) at line 57 \u2014 a raw JDBC Statement execution, not a PreparedStatement \u2014 with no escaping, parameterization, or validation applied to 'bar' anywhere in the shown code path. No sanitizer (ESAPI encoder, input validator, etc.) is applied before the SQL sink; ESAPI encoding is only used later for HTML output in printResults, which is irrelevant to SQL injection protection.",
