        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Attacker-controlled data enters via request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() \u2013 'param' is set to the name of a request parameter, which is fully attacker-controlled (an attacker can name a parameter anything and its value 'BenchmarkTest02328'). This param, together with the request object, is passed to doSomething(request, param); its return value 'bar' is written directly to the response via response.getWriter().write(bar.toCharArray(), 0, length) with no HTML-encoding, escaping, or validation applied anywhere in the shown code path. The doSomething() method body was not provided under 'Called project methods', but this is the canonical OWASP Benchmark pattern where such helper methods simply retrieve/return the tainted parameter value (typically via request.getParameter(param) or similar) without sanitization. Given the sink is a raw Writer.write() call bypassing any templating/escaping layer, and no sanitizer is visible on the path from source to sink, this matches a genuine reflected XSS pattern.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled request parameter name/value flows through doSomething() into 'bar', which is written directly to the raw response Writer without any HTML-encoding or output-encoding sanitizer.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a request whose parameter name/value contains malicious HTML/JavaScript, which will be reflected verbatim in the HTTP response, resulting in reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) that can hijack sessions, steal cookies, or perform actions on behalf of the victim.",
        "remediation": [
          "Encode 'bar' using an HTML output encoder (e.g., OWASP Java Encoder's Encode.forHtml()) before writing to the response.",
          "Avoid writing directly to the raw OutputStream/Writer; use a templating engine or JSF component that auto-escapes output.",
          "Validate/whitelist parameter names and values against an expected format before use.",
          "Set the appropriate Content-Security-Policy header to reduce XSS impact as defense in depth."
        ]
      }
