      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: HTTP request parameters via request.getParameterNames()/getParameterValues() \u2014 the code finds the parameter name whose value equals the marker string and stores it in 'param' (attacker-controlled parameter name). This name is passed to doSomething(request, param), whose body is not shown here but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper canonically resolves to 'return request.getParameter(param);' i.e. returns the raw, attacker-supplied value with no encoding/validation. The returned value 'bar' is concatenated directly into a shell command string ('echo ' + bar) which is added as a single argument to argList along with 'sh'/'-c' (or 'cmd.exe'/'/c') and passed to ProcessBuilder.command(argList) at line 76, then pb.start() executes it. Because the payload is executed through a shell (-c), any shell metacharacters (;, |, `` ` ``, $(), &&, etc.) in the parameter value will be interpreted by the shell, enabling arbitrary command injection. No sanitizer, allow-list validator, or escaping of shell metacharacters is applied anywhere on this path (Utils.printOSCommandResults only HTML-encodes the *output* for display, which does not mitigate the injection that already occurred).",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter value is passed unsanitized into a shell command line ('sh -c ...' / 'cmd.exe /c ...') built via string concatenation and executed with ProcessBuilder, allowing shell metacharacter injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary OS commands executed with the privileges of the web application process, leading to remote code execution, data exfiltration, or full host compromise.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell interpreter (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with concatenated user input; instead pass the command and each argument as separate ProcessBuilder list elements without a shell wrapper.",
          "Validate/allow-list the user-supplied value against a strict pattern (e.g., alphanumeric only) before using it in any command context.",
          "Use ESAPI or a dedicated OS-command encoder/validator to strip or reject shell metacharacters before use.",
          "Where possible, avoid shelling out entirely and use in-process Java APIs to accomplish the intended action."
        ]
      }
