        "impact": "An attacker able to control the parameter name of a request could inject additional command arguments or shell metacharacters, potentially resulting in arbitrary command execution on the host running the application, leading to full system compromise, data exfiltration, or denial of service.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking OS commands with user-influenced input; use safe Java APIs (e.g., java.nio.file for file operations) instead of shelling out.",
          "If exec is unavoidable, use a strict allow-list of permitted values and reject/escape any input containing shell metacharacters.",
          "Pass command arguments as a String[] to ProcessBuilder rather than concatenating a single command string, and never place attacker-controlled data as the executable path or first argument.",
          "Perform strict input validation on parameter names/values before using them in any sensitive sink."
        ]
      }
