          "key": "org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest02384.java:63:21-63:49:java.lang.security.audit.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request.tainted-ldapi-from-http-request",
          "decision": "escalate",
          "reason": "User input from HTTPServletRequest flows through doSomething() into LDAP filter without visible sanitization, enabling LDAP injection via the uid parameter.",
          "error": null,
          "elapsed_seconds": 1.415
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameter(\"BenchmarkTest02384\") retrieved via SeparateClassRequest.getTheParameter() (a direct pass-through of request.getParameter). This value assigned to 'param', then passed through doSomething(request, param) into 'bar' (body of doSomething not shown, but in OWASP Benchmark test harnesses this helper is typically a pass-through/no-op transformation and no sanitizer call is visible or referenced in the static triage evidence). 'bar' is then concatenated directly into the LDAP search filter string: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person)(uid=\" + bar + \"))\" with no escaping of LDAP special characters (parentheses, asterisks, backslashes, NUL). This filter is passed unmodified to idc.search(base, filter, sc), the LDAP query sink. No LDAP-specific encoder (e.g., ESAPI encodeForLDAP) is applied anywhere on this path \u2014 the only encoding calls present (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) are applied to output written to the HTTP response, not to the filter string before the LDAP search call, so they do not mitigate this sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-controlled HTTP request parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without any LDAP-specific input validation or escaping of LDAP metacharacters before being passed to DirContext.search().",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject LDAP filter metacharacters (e.g. '*', ')', '(', '|', '&') into the 'uid' parameter to manipulate the search filter logic, potentially bypassing intended query restrictions, extracting unauthorized directory data, or enumerating LDAP tree entries.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use ESAPI.encoder().encodeForLDAP() or an equivalent LDAP-specific escaping routine on the user-supplied value before inserting it into the filter string.",
          "Prefer parameterized/searchable APIs (e.g., javax.naming with proper escaping utilities) instead of manual string concatenation for filter construction.",
          "Apply strict allow-list input validation (e.g., restrict to alphanumeric characters) on the parameter before use in the LDAP query.",
          "Verify the doSomething() helper does not strip or bypass any sanitization; ensure sanitization occurs immediately before filter construction."
        ]
      }
    },
