        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02462\") is attacker-controlled and assigned to 'param'. It is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown in this context, and the return value ('bar') is used directly, unsanitized, as the second argument to 'new java.io.File(new java.io.File(TESTFILES_DIR), bar)' \u2014 the flagged path-traversal sink. The only encoding present in the method, ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML(fileTarget.toString()), is applied afterward purely to the HTML output message and does not sanitize or canonicalize the path used to construct/query the File object. No path validation (e.g., canonicalization + prefix check, FilenameUtils.getName, or a whitelist) is applied to 'bar' before it reaches the File constructor, so an attacker supplying '../' sequences can influence which file is checked with fileTarget.exists(), enabling path traversal / file existence disclosure outside TESTFILES_DIR.",
