        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter flows through an unshown pass-through helper (doSomething) directly into a java.io.File path construction without any canonicalization, normalization, or restriction to a safe base directory before the file is used in a filesystem existence check.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft the request parameter with directory traversal sequences (e.g., '../../etc/passwd') to make the application check for or reference files outside the intended TESTFILES_DIR, potentially disclosing filesystem structure/existence of arbitrary files and, in variants of this sink pattern, enabling further file read/write vulnerabilities.",
