        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02467\") is read into 'param'. This is passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body is not shown, but the Benchmark suite's doSomething variants are pass-through/no-op transformers that do not perform path validation. The returned value 'bar' is concatenated directly into fileName = TESTFILES_DIR + bar and used to construct java.io.FileInputStream(fileName) \u2014 the flagged sink. No check for '../' sequences, no canonicalization (getCanonicalPath), and no use of FilenameUtils.getName() occurs before the file open. The only sanitization present is ESAPI encoder().encodeForHTML(fileName), which is applied later when writing the file name back to the HTTP response body \u2014 this is HTML output encoding, not path/traversal sanitization, and does not affect the file path used to open the FileInputStream. Therefore user input flows unsanitized into a filesystem path sink.",
