      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02472\") -> param. param is passed into doSomething(request, param) (body not shown, but per OWASP Benchmark convention this is a pass-through/taint-preserving helper) and assigned to 'bar'. 'bar' is then directly string-concatenated into the LDAP filter: filter = \"(&(objectclass=person))(|(uid=\" + bar + \")(street={0}))\". This filter string is passed as the raw filter expression to idc.search(base, filter, filters, sc). The only sanitization present (ESAPI encodeForHTML) is applied later when writing results to the HTTP response, which protects against XSS, not LDAP injection \u2014 it does not sanitize 'bar' before it is embedded in the LDAP filter. No LDAP-specific encoding (e.g., escaping *, (, ), \\, NUL) is applied to 'bar' prior to the search call. This is a direct, unsanitized taint flow into an LDAP query sink.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into an LDAP search filter string without LDAP-specific escaping or use of parameterized filter arguments, allowing filter syntax injection.",
        "impact": "An attacker can manipulate the LDAP query logic via the 'BenchmarkTest02472' parameter (e.g., injecting characters like ')(uid=*)(|(uid=*' or wildcard/filter metacharacters) to bypass intended filter constraints, enumerate or exfiltrate LDAP directory entries, or otherwise tamper with search semantics \u2014 classic LDAP injection (CWE-90).",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized LDAP search filters by passing all user-controlled values via the filter arguments array (as already done for the 'street' attribute with {0}) instead of string concatenation.",
          "Apply proper LDAP filter escaping to the 'bar' value (escape '(', ')', '\\\\', '*', and NUL characters) before including it in the filter string, e.g., using ESAPI's encodeForLDAP or a dedicated LDAP escaping utility.",
          "Validate/allowlist the expected format of the 'BenchmarkTest02472' parameter before use in the query."
        ]
      }
    },
