        "remediation": [
          "Never pass unsanitized user input into Runtime.exec/ProcessBuilder in any position \u2014 command array, arguments, or environment array.",
          "If environment customization is required, validate and whitelist allowed variable names and values (e.g., only allow a small fixed set of key=value pairs).",
          "Avoid replacing the full child process environment with user-influenced data; explicitly construct envp from trusted, hard-coded values only.",
          "Prefer ProcessBuilder with explicit argument lists and avoid shell/script indirection so environment-based attack surface (PATH hijacking, LD_PRELOAD, etc.) is minimized.",
          "Run subprocess with a minimal, fixed environment and drop unnecessary privileges."
        ]
      }
