        "severity_assessment": "low",
        "root_cause": "The Semgrep rule pattern-matches any HTTP-request-derived value flowing near a Runtime.exec/ProcessBuilder call, but does not distinguish which exec overload is used. Here Runtime.exec(String command, String[] envp) is used, so the tainted array is consumed as environment variables for the child process rather than as the executed command or its arguments, which is a fundamentally different (and in this configuration non-exploitable) sink for OS command injection.",
