      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02525\") is read into `param` (attacker-controlled, no validation applied to the array elements). This value is passed to `bar = doSomething(request, param)`; the body of doSomething is not shown/resolved, but nothing on the visible path performs input validation before the sink. `bar` is then passed directly to `request.getSession().putValue(\"userid\", bar)` at line 51, storing raw/attacker-influenced data as a session attribute. The only sanitizer present, `Utils.encodeForHTML(bar)`, is applied afterward solely to the value written to the HTTP response body (output encoding for HTML context) \u2014 it is never applied to the value stored in the session, so it does not protect the putValue sink. Because the session now holds unvalidated request-derived data that other code may later trust, the trust-boundary violation sink is reached without any adequate sanitizer for that specific sink.",
