      "analysis": {
        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02530\") stores attacker-controlled input into 'param'. This is passed to bar = doSomething(request, param); while doSomething's body is not shown, in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper is a pass-through/no-op wrapper that returns the tainted value unmodified (no validation/encoding). 'bar' is then directly concatenated into the SQL command string: String sql = \"{call \" + bar + \"}\"; This raw string is passed to connection.prepareCall(sql, ...) and executed via statement.executeQuery(). There is no use of bind parameters, no allow-list validation, and no escaping of 'bar' before it is embedded into the SQL command text. The only encoding present (ESAPI.encoder().encodeForHTML) is applied later to output in printResults, which protects against XSS on the response, not SQL injection on the query construction. Therefore the tainted value reaches the SQL sink unsanitized.",
        "verdict": "True Positive",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied HTTP parameter is concatenated directly into a SQL/CallableStatement string without parameterization or validation before being executed against the database.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL/stored-procedure call syntax via the 'BenchmarkTest02530' parameter, potentially allowing data exfiltration, modification, or execution of unintended stored procedures/commands on the backend database.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use parameterized queries (PreparedStatement/CallableStatement with '?' placeholders and setString/setInt etc.) instead of string concatenation for the SQL/call statement.",
          "If a stored procedure name or dynamic SQL fragment must be built from user input, validate it against a strict allow-list of expected values.",
          "Apply the principle of least privilege to the database account used by the application to limit the impact of any injection.",
          "Enable logging/alerting on anomalous SQL statements for early detection of injection attempts."
        ]
      }
    },
