        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getParameterValues(\"BenchmarkTest02545\") assigned to param (attacker-controlled HTTP parameter). param is passed to doSomething(request, param) and returned as bar; the body of doSomething is not shown but is not listed among sanitizing helper methods, and in this codebase such helper typically returns the value unchanged. bar is concatenated directly into the SQL string: \"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES ('foo','\" + bar + \"')\" with no escaping or parameterization, then executed via statement.executeUpdate(sql) using a plain java.sql.Statement (not PreparedStatement). No sanitizer, allow-list validator, or SQL escaping is applied anywhere on this path before the sink.",
