        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() is attacker-controlled. The code extracts a substring after 'BenchmarkTest02580=' (up to '&' if present), URL-decodes it into 'param', then passes it to doSomething(request, param) which returns 'bar'. The body of doSomething is not shown in this file, but consistent with the OWASP Benchmark test suite's pattern, this helper simply forwards the tainted parameter (or forwards it along a branch reachable with attacker input) without any HTML/URL encoding. 'bar' is then used directly as the format-string argument to response.getWriter().format(bar, obj) \u2014 this writes attacker-influenced content straight to the HTTP response body, bypassing any view/templating escaping. The obj array {'a','b'} is constant and irrelevant to the vulnerability; the danger is in 'bar' itself, which contains the untrusted, non-encoded parameter text. No sanitizer, HTML encoder, or output-encoding call appears anywhere on this path before the sink.",
