        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> extracted substring 'param' -> URL-decoded via URLDecoder.decode -> passed into doSomething(request, param) -> result 'bar' returned and written directly to response.getWriter().print(bar) at line 73 with no HTML encoding, escaping, or output-encoding applied. The doSomething() method body is not shown in this context, so no sanitizer can be confirmed on the path; the value written to the OutputStream is fully attacker-controlled via the query string and reflected unmodified aside from URL decoding, which does not neutralize HTML/script metacharacters. No adequate encoder for an HTML sink is applied before response.getWriter().print(bar).",
