        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "medium",
        "root_cause": "The servletet directly writes a value derived from an unsecured, URL-decoquery-string parameter to the response'sream via any Houtput encoding, bypassing any view/template escaping. Whether doSsomething() performs sanitization cannot be verified from the code shown, but no evidence of sanitization is present on the observable path, so the reflected XSS pattern is realized at the print() sink.",
        "impact": "An attacker can craft a URL with a malicious script payload in the query string parameter; when a victim clicks the link, the payload is reflected back and executed in the victim's browser context, enabling session hijacking, credential theft, or other client-side attacks (reflected XSS).",
