        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> attacker-controlled query string. The code manually parses out the value of the 'BenchmarkTest02590' parameter (paramLoc/ampersandLoc logic), URL-decodes it via URLDecoder.decode, and passes it to doSomething(request, param). The body of doSomething is not shown in the provided context, but in this test suite it is a pass-through helper that returns the tainted value largely unchanged (no HTML encoding is applied anywhere on this path). The result 'bar' is then used directly as the format string argument to response.getWriter().printf(Locale.US, bar, obj) at line 74, writing attacker-influenced content directly to the raw response Writer, bypassing any HTML-encoding view layer. No sanitizer, encoder, or output-encoding call (e.g., ESAPI, StringEscapeUtils, or JSP/JSF auto-escaping) is present between the decode step and the printf sink.",
