        "exploitability_evidence": "Source: request.getQueryString() -> extracted substring 'param' -> URLDecoder.decode(param, 'UTF-8') (still attacker-controlled, decoding does not neutralize HTML/script characters) -> passed to doSomething(request, param) whose body isn't shown but in the OWASP Benchmark suite this helper is typically a pass-through/transform that preserves the injected payload -> result 'bar' concatenated into a string and written directly via response.getWriter().write(\"Parameter value: \" + bar) with no HTML encoding, output escaping, or allow-list validation applied anywhere on the path. The sink is a raw Writer.write() call, bypassing any templating escaping. No sanitizer neutralizes '<', '>', '\"', or other HTML-significant characters before the sink.",
