        "confidence": "medium",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string parameter is decoded and concatenated directly into a shell command string executed via Runtime.exec with 'sh -c', without any validation, whitelist, or shell-metacharacter escaping.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary shell commands via the query parameter, potentially leading to remote code execution, data exfiltration, or full server compromise.",
        "remediation": [
          "Avoid invoking a shell (sh -c / cmd.exe /c) with untrusted input; use ProcessBuilder with an argument list and no shell interpretation.",
          "Validate the input against a strict whitelist of allowed characters/values before use in any command.",
          "If shell functionality is required, use a well-tested escaping library or API designed for safe command construction, and reject inputs containing metacharacters like ; | & ` $ ( ) etc.",
          "Prefer high-level Java APIs over shelling out to OS commands entirely where possible."
        ]
      }
