        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied input from the HTTP query string is concatenated directly into a SQL query string instead of being bound as a parameter; only part of the query (USERNAME) is parameterized, while the PASSWORD portion embeds tainted input as a literal string in the SQL text, allowing SQL injection via crafted query string values (e.g., closing the quote and injecting SQL).",
