        "remediation": [
          "Bind the PASSWORD value as a query parameter using a placeholder (e.g., `AND PASSWORD=?`) and set it via `statement.setString(2, bar)` instead of string concatenation.",
          "Avoid building any part of the SQL text from unsanitized user input; use fully parameterized queries for all variable values.",
          "If dynamic column/table names are unavoidable, use a strict allow-list validator, but never for literal values that can be parameterized.",
          "Apply input validation/normalization for the decoded parameter to reject unexpected characters (e.g., quotes) as defense in depth."
        ]
