        "confidence": "high",
        "severity_assessment": "high",
        "root_cause": "User-supplied query string parameter is URL-decoded and concatenated directly into a SQL query string, which is then executed via Statement.execute() instead of using a parameterized PreparedStatement, allowing SQL metacharacters (e.g., a single quote) to alter query semantics.",
        "impact": "An attacker can inject arbitrary SQL via the URL query parameter to bypass authentication, extract or modify data from the USERS table, or potentially escalate to broader database compromise depending on DB permissions.",
        "remediation": [
          "Use java.sql.PreparedStatement with parameterized queries (?, placeholders) instead of building SQL via string concatenation.",
          "Bind the 'bar' value using setString() rather than embedding it directly in the SQL text.",
          "Apply strict input validation/allow-listing on the parameter if it is expected to be a simple username/password value.",
          "Avoid using Statement.execute() with dynamically built SQL strings for user-controlled input."
        ]
      }
